window.CGL_DATA=window.CGL_DATA||{};window.CGL_DATA["CGL-06-OCT-2026-SHIFT-2"]={"id":"CGL-06-OCT-2026-SHIFT-2","title":"CGL 06 OCT 2026 SHIFT 2","order":["REASONING","GK","MATH","ENGLISH"],"marking":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"qualifying":[],"sections":{"REASONING":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":1,"local_id":"50001","quid":"Q1000072381","section":"REASONING","topic":"Number Analogy","question":{"en":"Find the missing number: 36 : 108 :: 49 : ? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"लुप्त संख्या ज्ञात कीजिए: 36 : 108 :: 49 : ? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"145"},"2":{"en":"147"},"3":{"en":"141"},"4":{"en":"146"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"The second number is three times the first number: 36 × 3 = 108 ✔<br>Applying the same relation, 49 × 3 = 147<br>Hence the missing number is 147<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 147.</b>","hi":"दूसरी संख्या पहली संख्या की तीन गुनी है: 36 × 3 = 108 ✔<br>वही संबंध लगाने पर 49 × 3 = 147<br>इसलिए लुप्त संख्या 147 है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 147 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":2,"local_id":"50002","quid":"Q1000072382","section":"REASONING","topic":"Miscellaneous","question":{"en":"A bag contains coins of Rs. 1, Rs. 2 and Rs. 5 in the ratio 5:3:2. If the total money is Rs. 420, find the number of Rs. 2 coins. [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"एक थैले में 1 रु., 2 रु. तथा 5 रु. के सिक्के 5:3:2 के अनुपात में हैं। यदि कुल धन 420 रु. है, तो 2 रु. के सिक्कों की संख्या ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"36"},"2":{"en":"28"},"3":{"en":"24"},"4":{"en":"60"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Let the numbers of coins be 5x, 3x and 2x<br>The value is 1 × 5x + 2 × 3x + 5 × 2x = 5x + 6x + 10x = 21x<br>21x = 420 gives x = 20<br>So the number of Rs. 2 coins is 3x = 60<br>Hence there are 60 coins of Rs. 2<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 60.</b>","hi":"मान लीजिए सिक्कों की संख्या 5x, 3x तथा 2x है<br>मूल्य है 1 × 5x + 2 × 3x + 5 × 2x = 5x + 6x + 10x = 21x<br>21x = 420 से x = 20 मिलता है<br>अतः 2 रु. के सिक्कों की संख्या 3x = 60 है<br>इसलिए 2 रु. के 60 सिक्के हैं<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 60 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":3,"local_id":"50003","quid":"Q1000072383","section":"REASONING","topic":"Syllogism","question":{"en":"Read the following statement carefully and identify the conclusion that follows.<br><b>Statement:</b> Some flowers are red. All red things are attractive.<br><b>Conclusions:</b><br>I. Some flowers are attractive.<br>II. All flowers are attractive. [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"निम्नलिखित कथन को ध्यान से पढ़िए और वह निष्कर्ष पहचानिए जो निकलता है।<br><b>कथन:</b> कुछ फूल लाल हैं। सभी लाल वस्तुएँ आकर्षक हैं।<br><b>निष्कर्ष:</b><br>I. कुछ फूल आकर्षक हैं।<br>II. सभी फूल आकर्षक हैं। [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only I follows","hi":"केवल I निकलता है"},"2":{"en":"Only II follows","hi":"केवल II निकलता है"},"3":{"en":"Both I and II follow","hi":"I और II दोनों निकलते हैं"},"4":{"en":"Neither I nor II follows","hi":"कोई नहीं निकलता"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Some flowers are red and all red things are attractive, so those flowers that are red are attractive ✔<br>This gives only 'some flowers are attractive' and not 'all flowers are attractive' ✘<br>Hence only conclusion I follows<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Only I follows.</b>","hi":"कुछ फूल लाल हैं और सभी लाल वस्तुएँ आकर्षक हैं, अतः जो फूल लाल हैं वे आकर्षक हैं ✔<br>इससे केवल 'कुछ फूल आकर्षक हैं' निकलता है, 'सभी फूल आकर्षक हैं' नहीं ✘<br>इसलिए केवल निष्कर्ष I निकलता है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): केवल I निकलता है है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":4,"local_id":"50004","quid":"Q1000072384","section":"REASONING","topic":"Number Series","question":{"en":"What is the next number in the series?<br>7, 21, 63, ___ [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"श्रेणी में अगली संख्या क्या है?<br>7, 21, 63, ___ [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"183"},"2":{"en":"190"},"3":{"en":"201"},"4":{"en":"189"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Every term is three times the term before it: 7 × 3 = 21 and 21 × 3 = 63 ✔<br>So the next term is 63 × 3 = 189<br>Hence the next number is 189<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 189.</b>","hi":"प्रत्येक पद अपने पहले पद का तीन गुना है: 7 × 3 = 21 तथा 21 × 3 = 63 ✔<br>अतः अगला पद 63 × 3 = 189 है<br>इसलिए अगली संख्या 189 है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 189 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":5,"local_id":"50005","quid":"Q1000072385","section":"REASONING","topic":"Blood Relations","question":{"en":"'A # B' means 'A is the brother of B'.<br>'A @ B' means 'A is the father of B'.<br>'A &amp; B' means 'A is the sister of B'.<br>'A % B' means 'A is the daughter of B'.<br>If 'T @ M &amp; F # R &amp; G % K', then how is K related to R? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"'A # B' का अर्थ है 'A, B का भाई है'।<br>'A @ B' का अर्थ है 'A, B का पिता है'।<br>'A &amp; B' का अर्थ है 'A, B की बहन है'।<br>'A % B' का अर्थ है 'A, B की पुत्री है'।<br>यदि 'T @ M &amp; F # R &amp; G % K' है, तो K, R से कैसे संबंधित है? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Mother","hi":"माता"},"2":{"en":"Father-in-law","hi":"ससुर"},"3":{"en":"Brother-in-law","hi":"साला/देवर"},"4":{"en":"Grandmother","hi":"दादी/नानी"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"293\" height=\"108\" viewBox=\"0 0 293 108\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><g fill=\"#fff3c4\" stroke=\"#e0a000\"><rect x=\"160\" y=\"8\" width=\"27\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\"/><rect x=\"159\" y=\"62\" width=\"27\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\"/></g><path d=\"M136 14H158M136 18H158M147 18V50M73 50H221M73 50V62M123 50V62M172 50V62M221 50V62\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"121\" y=\"22\">T+</text><text x=\"173\" y=\"22\">K−</text><text x=\"73\" y=\"76\">M−</text><text x=\"123\" y=\"76\">F+</text><text x=\"172\" y=\"76\">R−</text><text x=\"221\" y=\"76\">G−</text></g><text x=\"146\" y=\"103\" fill=\"#555\" stroke=\"none\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">+ Male  − Female  — Sibling  = Couple  | Generation</text></svg><br>M, F, R and G are siblings and T is their father; K is a parent of G other than T, so K is their mother.<br>Hence K is the mother of R.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Mother.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"293\" height=\"108\" viewBox=\"0 0 293 108\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><g fill=\"#fff3c4\" stroke=\"#e0a000\"><rect x=\"160\" y=\"8\" width=\"27\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\"/><rect x=\"159\" y=\"62\" width=\"27\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\"/></g><path d=\"M136 14H158M136 18H158M147 18V50M73 50H221M73 50V62M123 50V62M172 50V62M221 50V62\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"121\" y=\"22\">T+</text><text x=\"173\" y=\"22\">K−</text><text x=\"73\" y=\"76\">M−</text><text x=\"123\" y=\"76\">F+</text><text x=\"172\" y=\"76\">R−</text><text x=\"221\" y=\"76\">G−</text></g><text x=\"146\" y=\"103\" fill=\"#555\" stroke=\"none\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">+ पुरुष  − स्त्री  — भाई-बहन  = पति-पत्नी  | पीढ़ी</text></svg><br>M, F, R तथा G भाई-बहन हैं और T उनका पिता है; K, G का T के अतिरिक्त अभिभावक है, अतः K उनकी माता है।<br>अतः K, R की माता है।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): माता है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":6,"local_id":"50006","quid":"Q1000072386","section":"REASONING","topic":"Mathematical Operations","question":{"en":"If '+' means '×', '−' means '+', '×' means '÷', and '÷' means '−', then 6 + 3 − 2 × 2 = ? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"यदि '+' का अर्थ '×', '−' का अर्थ '+', '×' का अर्थ '÷' तथा '÷' का अर्थ '−' है, तो 6 + 3 − 2 × 2 = ? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"15"},"2":{"en":"20"},"3":{"en":"12"},"4":{"en":"19"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"After substitution the expression becomes 6 × 3 + 2 ÷ 2<br>6 × 3 = 18 and 2 ÷ 2 = 1<br>So the value is 18 + 1 = 19<br>Hence the value is 19<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 19.</b>","hi":"प्रतिस्थापन के बाद व्यंजक 6 × 3 + 2 ÷ 2 बनता है<br>6 × 3 = 18 तथा 2 ÷ 2 = 1<br>अतः मान 18 + 1 = 19 है<br>इसलिए मान 19 है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 19 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":7,"local_id":"50007","quid":"Q1000072387","section":"REASONING","topic":"Coding & Decoding","question":{"en":"If \"HOUSE\" is coded as 8-15-21-19-5, how will \"SHOE\" be coded? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"यदि \"HOUSE\" का कूट 8-15-21-19-5 है, तो \"SHOE\" का कूट क्या होगा? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"19-8-15-5"},"2":{"en":"19-8-5-15"},"3":{"en":"8-19-15-5"},"4":{"en":"8-15-19-5"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Each letter is replaced by its position in the alphabet: H = 8, O = 15, U = 21, S = 19 and E = 5 ✔<br>For SHOE the positions are S = 19, H = 8, O = 15 and E = 5<br>Hence SHOE is coded as 19-8-15-5<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 19-8-15-5.</b>","hi":"प्रत्येक अक्षर को वर्णमाला में उसके स्थान से बदला जाता है: H = 8, O = 15, U = 21, S = 19 तथा E = 5 ✔<br>SHOE के लिए स्थान हैं S = 19, H = 8, O = 15 तथा E = 5<br>इसलिए SHOE का कूट 19-8-15-5 है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 19-8-15-5 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":8,"local_id":"50008","quid":"Q1000072388","section":"REASONING","topic":"Coding & Decoding","question":{"en":"In a certain code language, \"APPLE\" is represented as \"ELPPA.\" What does \"MANGO\" look like in that code? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"एक निश्चित कूट भाषा में \"APPLE\" को \"ELPPA\" लिखा जाता है। उस कूट में \"MANGO\" कैसा दिखेगा? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"OGNAM"},"2":{"en":"ONMAG"},"3":{"en":"MANGO G"},"4":{"en":"OGAMN"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"ELPPA is APPLE written in the reverse order ✔<br>Reversing MANGO gives OGNAM<br>Hence MANGO is written as OGNAM<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): OGNAM.</b>","hi":"ELPPA, APPLE को उल्टे क्रम में लिखा गया रूप है ✔<br>MANGO को उल्टा करने पर OGNAM मिलता है<br>इसलिए MANGO को OGNAM लिखा जाएगा<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): OGNAM है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":9,"local_id":"50009","quid":"Q1000072389","section":"REASONING","topic":"Address/Sentence Matching","question":{"en":"<b>Which of the following alternatives matches the given address exactly?</b><br>Mr. R. Khanna<br>Flat No. 1204, Silver Crest Towers, 11th Floor, Sector 62<br>Noida, Uttar Pradesh - 201309<br><b>Alternatives:</b><br>A) Mr. R. Khanna, Flat No. 1204, Silver Crest Towers, 11th Floor, Sector 62, Noida, Uttar Pradesh - 201309<br>B) Mr. R. Khanna, Flat No. 1204, Silver Crest Towers, 11th Floor, Sector 64, Noida, Uttar Pradesh - 201309<br>C) Mr. R. Khanna, Flat No. 1204, Silver Crest Towers, 11th Floor, Sector 62, Noida, Uttar Pradesh - 201309<br>D) Mr. R. Khanna, Flat No. 1204, Silver Crest Towers, 12th Floor, Sector 62, Noida, Uttar Pradesh - 201309<br>E) Mr. R. Khanna, Flat No. 1204, Silver Crest Towers, 11th Floor, Sector 26, Noida, Uttar Pradesh - 201309<br>F) Mr. R. Khanna, Flat No. 1204, Silver Crest Towers, 11th Floor, Sector 62, Noida, Uttar Pradesh - 201390 [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"<b>निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा विकल्प दिए गए पते से पूरी तरह मेल खाता है?</b><br>Mr. R. Khanna<br>Flat No. 1204, Silver Crest Towers, 11th Floor, Sector 62<br>Noida, Uttar Pradesh - 201309<br><b>विकल्प:</b><br>A) Mr. R. Khanna, Flat No. 1204, Silver Crest Towers, 11th Floor, Sector 62, Noida, Uttar Pradesh - 201309<br>B) Mr. R. Khanna, Flat No. 1204, Silver Crest Towers, 11th Floor, Sector 64, Noida, Uttar Pradesh - 201309<br>C) Mr. R. Khanna, Flat No. 1204, Silver Crest Towers, 11th Floor, Sector 62, Noida, Uttar Pradesh - 201309<br>D) Mr. R. Khanna, Flat No. 1204, Silver Crest Towers, 12th Floor, Sector 62, Noida, Uttar Pradesh - 201309<br>E) Mr. R. Khanna, Flat No. 1204, Silver Crest Towers, 11th Floor, Sector 26, Noida, Uttar Pradesh - 201309<br>F) Mr. R. Khanna, Flat No. 1204, Silver Crest Towers, 11th Floor, Sector 62, Noida, Uttar Pradesh - 201390 [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"A and C","hi":"A और C"},"2":{"en":"C and E","hi":"C और E"},"3":{"en":"A and F","hi":"A और F"},"4":{"en":"D and B","hi":"D और B"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Options A and C repeat the given address word for word, with the same flat number, floor, sector and PIN 201309 ✔<br>Option B changes the sector to 64, option D changes the floor to 12th, option E changes the sector to 26 and option F changes the PIN to 201390 ✘<br>Hence A and C exactly match the given address<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): A and C.</b>","hi":"विकल्प A तथा C दिया गया पता शब्द-प्रति-शब्द दोहराते हैं, उसी फ्लैट संख्या, मंजिल, सेक्टर तथा पिन 201309 के साथ ✔<br>विकल्प B में सेक्टर 64, विकल्प D में मंजिल 12th, विकल्प E में सेक्टर 26 तथा विकल्प F में पिन 201390 हो जाता है ✘<br>इसलिए A तथा C दिए गए पते से पूरी तरह मेल खाते हैं<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): A और C है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":10,"local_id":"50010","quid":"Q1000072390","section":"REASONING","topic":"Coding & Decoding","question":{"en":"In a certain code language, \"COMPUTATION\" is written as \"OOITATUPMOD\". How will \"RECOGNITION\" be written? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"एक निश्चित कूट भाषा में \"COMPUTATION\" को \"OOITATUPMOD\" लिखा जाता है। \"RECOGNITION\" कैसे लिखा जाएगा? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"OIOTINGCOES"},"2":{"en":"OOITINGOCES"},"3":{"en":"NOIITNGCOER"},"4":{"en":"NOTIINCGOER"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"COMPUTATION written backwards reads N O I T A T U P M O C<br>In the code only the first letter of this reversed word moves one place ahead (N→O) and the last letter moves one place ahead (C→D): O O I T A T U P M O D ✔<br>RECOGNITION backwards reads N O I T I N G O C E R<br>N→O and R→S give O O I T I N G O C E S<br>Hence RECOGNITION is written as OOITINGOCES<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): OOITINGOCES.</b>","hi":"COMPUTATION को उल्टा लिखने पर N O I T A T U P M O C मिलता है<br>कूट में इस उल्टे शब्द का केवल पहला अक्षर एक स्थान आगे (N→O) तथा अंतिम अक्षर एक स्थान आगे (C→D) होता है: O O I T A T U P M O D ✔<br>RECOGNITION को उल्टा लिखने पर N O I T I N G O C E R<br>N→O तथा R→S करने पर O O I T I N G O C E S<br>इसलिए RECOGNITION को OOITINGOCES लिखा जाएगा<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): OOITINGOCES है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":11,"local_id":"50011","quid":"Q1000072391","section":"REASONING","topic":"Address/Sentence Matching","question":{"en":"<b>Choose the option that perfectly matches the given address.</b><br><b>Original Address:</b><br>Flat No. &#937;-17/BRésidence d'Élite, Tower-XIVSt. Michael's Crescent, Sector-09Navi Mumbai, Maharashtra 400706India | Asia [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"<b>वह विकल्प चुनिए जो दिए गए पते से पूरी तरह मेल खाता है।</b><br><b>मूल पता:</b><br>Flat No. &#937;-17/BRésidence d'Élite, Tower-XIVSt. Michael's Crescent, Sector-09Navi Mumbai, Maharashtra 400706India | Asia [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Flat No. &#937;-17/BRésidence d'Elite, Tower-XIVSt. Michael's Crescent, Sector-09Navi Mumbai, Maharashtra 400706India | Asia"},"2":{"en":"Flat No. &#937;-17-BRésidence d'Élite, Tower-XIVSt. Michael's Crescent, Sector-09Navi Mumbai, Maharashtra 400706India | Asia"},"3":{"en":"Flat No. &#937;-17/BRésidence d'Élite, Tower-XIVSt. Michael's Crescent, Sector-09Navi Mumbai, Maharashtra 400760India | Asia"},"4":{"en":"Flat No. &#937;-17/BRésidence d'Élite, Tower-XIVSt. Michael's Crescent, Sector-09Navi Mumbai, Maharashtra 400706India | Asia"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Option D keeps every part of the address exactly: the Omega symbol, '17/B', the accented word Élite, Tower-XIV, Sector-09, PIN 400706 and 'India | Asia' ✔<br>Option A drops the accent on Elite, option B changes the slash to a hyphen and option C changes the PIN to 400760 ✘<br>Hence option D perfectly matches the given address<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): Flat No. &#937;-17/BRésidence d'Élite, Tower-XIVSt. Michael's Crescent, Sector-09Navi Mumbai, Maharashtra 400706India | Asia.</b>","hi":"विकल्प D पते का प्रत्येक भाग ठीक वैसा ही रखता है: ओमेगा चिह्न, '17/B', उच्चारण-चिह्न वाला शब्द Élite, Tower-XIV, Sector-09, पिन 400706 तथा 'India | Asia' ✔<br>विकल्प A में Elite पर उच्चारण-चिह्न हट जाता है, विकल्प B में स्लैश के स्थान पर हाइफ़न आ जाता है और विकल्प C में पिन 400760 हो जाता है ✘<br>इसलिए विकल्प D दिए गए पते से पूरी तरह मेल खाता है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): Flat No. &#937;-17/BRésidence d'Élite, Tower-XIVSt. Michael's Crescent, Sector-09Navi Mumbai, Maharashtra 400706India | Asia है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":12,"local_id":"50012","quid":"Q1000072392","section":"REASONING","topic":"Blood Relations","question":{"en":"If 'A &#36; B' means 'A is the brother of B', 'A # B' means 'A is the mother of B', and 'A * B' means 'A is the daughter of B', which of the following options means 'M is the maternal uncle of N'? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"यदि 'A &#36; B' का अर्थ है 'A, B का भाई है', 'A # B' का अर्थ है 'A, B की माता है' तथा 'A * B' का अर्थ है 'A, B की पुत्री है', तो निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा विकल्प 'M, N का मामा है' दर्शाता है? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"M &#36; O # N"},"2":{"en":"M &#36; O * N"},"3":{"en":"M # O &#36; N"},"4":{"en":"M * O &#36; N"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"293\" height=\"134\" viewBox=\"0 0 293 134\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><g fill=\"#fff3c4\" stroke=\"#e0a000\"><rect x=\"108\" y=\"34\" width=\"29\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\"/><rect x=\"162\" y=\"88\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\"/></g><path d=\"M172 54V76M172 76V88M122 24H172M122 24V34M172 24V34\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"122\" y=\"48\">M+</text><text x=\"172\" y=\"48\">O−</text><text x=\"172\" y=\"102\">N</text></g><text x=\"146\" y=\"129\" fill=\"#555\" stroke=\"none\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">+ Male  − Female  — Sibling  = Couple  | Generation</text></svg><br>M &#36; O # N: M is the brother of O, and O is the mother of N, so M is the maternal uncle of N.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): M &#36; O # N.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"293\" height=\"134\" viewBox=\"0 0 293 134\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><g fill=\"#fff3c4\" stroke=\"#e0a000\"><rect x=\"108\" y=\"34\" width=\"29\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\"/><rect x=\"162\" y=\"88\" width=\"20\" height=\"20\" rx=\"4\"/></g><path d=\"M172 54V76M172 76V88M122 24H172M122 24V34M172 24V34\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"none\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"122\" y=\"48\">M+</text><text x=\"172\" y=\"48\">O−</text><text x=\"172\" y=\"102\">N</text></g><text x=\"146\" y=\"129\" fill=\"#555\" stroke=\"none\" font-size=\"10\" text-anchor=\"middle\">+ पुरुष  − स्त्री  — भाई-बहन  = पति-पत्नी  | पीढ़ी</text></svg><br>M &#36; O # N: M, O का भाई है तथा O, N की माता है, अतः M, N का मामा है।<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): M &#36; O # N है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":13,"local_id":"50013","quid":"Q1000072393","section":"REASONING","topic":"Miscellaneous","question":{"en":"A batch of roll numbers follows the pattern [Even Number]-[Odd Number]-[Even Number] for the first three digits. Identify the invalid roll number. [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"रोल नंबरों का एक समूह पहले तीन अंकों के लिए [सम संख्या]-[विषम संख्या]-[सम संख्या] का पैटर्न अपनाता है। अमान्य रोल नंबर पहचानिए। [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"694-11-22"},"2":{"en":"472-99-05"},"3":{"en":"258-44-11"},"4":{"en":"386-55-10"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"The first three digits must be Even – Odd – Even<br>694 → 6 even, 9 odd, 4 even ✔<br>472 → 4 even, 7 odd, 2 even ✔<br>258 → 2 even, 5 odd, 8 even ✔<br>386 → 3 is odd, 8 is even, 6 even ✘<br>So 386-55-10 breaks the pattern<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 386-55-10.</b>","hi":"पहले तीन अंक सम – विषम – सम होने चाहिए<br>694 → 6 सम, 9 विषम, 4 सम ✔<br>472 → 4 सम, 7 विषम, 2 सम ✔<br>258 → 2 सम, 5 विषम, 8 सम ✔<br>386 → 3 विषम है, 8 सम है, 6 सम ✘<br>अतः 386-55-10 पैटर्न का पालन नहीं करता<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 386-55-10 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":14,"local_id":"50014","quid":"Q1000072394","section":"REASONING","topic":"Letter & Alphanumeric Series","question":{"en":"Study the pattern in the given series and find the next set of letters in the series.<br>DHI, HGM, LFQ, ? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"दी गई श्रेणी का पैटर्न देखिए और श्रेणी में अगला अक्षर-समूह ज्ञात कीजिए।<br>DHI, HGM, LFQ, ? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"PEU"},"2":{"en":"PDU"},"3":{"en":"PEV"},"4":{"en":"PET"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"The first letters D, H, L move four places ahead each time, so the next first letter is P ✔<br>The second letters H, G, F move one place back each time, so the next second letter is E ✔<br>The third letters I, M, Q move four places ahead each time, so the next third letter is U<br>Hence the next cluster is PEU<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): PEU.</b>","hi":"पहले अक्षर D, H, L प्रत्येक बार चार स्थान आगे बढ़ते हैं, अतः अगला पहला अक्षर P है ✔<br>दूसरे अक्षर H, G, F प्रत्येक बार एक स्थान पीछे जाते हैं, अतः अगला दूसरा अक्षर E है ✔<br>तीसरे अक्षर I, M, Q प्रत्येक बार चार स्थान आगे बढ़ते हैं, अतः अगला तीसरा अक्षर U है<br>इसलिए अगला समूह PEU है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): PEU है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":15,"local_id":"50015","quid":"Q1000072395","section":"REASONING","topic":"Missing Number","question":{"en":"In the following question, a matrix of numbers is given. These numbers follow a certain pattern either row-wise or column-wise. Identify this pattern and choose the missing number accordingly.<br><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse\"><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">50</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">33</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">47</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">62</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">44</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">58</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">39</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">?</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">36</td></tr></table> [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"निम्नलिखित प्रश्न में संख्याओं का एक आव्यूह दिया गया है। ये संख्याएँ पंक्ति-वार या स्तंभ-वार किसी निश्चित पैटर्न का पालन करती हैं। यह पैटर्न पहचानिए और उसके अनुसार लुप्त संख्या चुनिए।<br><table style=\"border-collapse:collapse\"><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">50</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">33</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">47</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">62</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">44</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">58</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">39</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">?</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #888;padding:3px 6px\">36</td></tr></table> [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"11"},"2":{"en":"22"},"3":{"en":"33"},"4":{"en":"44"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"In each row, middle number = (first number − third number) × 11<br>(50 − 47) × 11 = 33 ✔<br>(62 − 58) × 11 = 44 ✔<br>(39 − 36) × 11 = 33<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 33.</b>","hi":"प्रत्येक पंक्ति में, बीच की संख्या = (पहली संख्या − तीसरी संख्या) × 11<br>(50 − 47) × 11 = 33 ✔<br>(62 − 58) × 11 = 44 ✔<br>(39 − 36) × 11 = 33<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 33 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":16,"local_id":"50016","quid":"Q1000072396","section":"REASONING","topic":"Situational Judgement","question":{"en":"Your superior, a highly demanding director, drops a massive, unvetted data analysis task on your desk at 5:30 PM, demanding the final report by 9:00 AM tomorrow. You already have a critical, pre-scheduled medical appointment for your dependent parent at 7:00 PM tonight. Which response represents the most emotionally intelligent negotiation? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"आपके वरिष्ठ, एक अत्यधिक अपेक्षा रखने वाले निदेशक, शाम 5:30 बजे आपके डेस्क पर डेटा विश्लेषण का बड़ा और बिना जाँचा-परखा कार्य डाल देते हैं और अगली सुबह 9:00 बजे तक अंतिम रिपोर्ट माँगते हैं। आपके आश्रित माता-पिता के लिए आज रात 7:00 बजे पहले से तय एक महत्वपूर्ण चिकित्सा अपॉइंटमेंट है। कौन-सी प्रतिक्रिया सर्वाधिक भावनात्मक रूप से बुद्धिमान बातचीत दर्शाती है? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Accept the task silently, cancel your parent's medical appointment, and stay up all night to finish it to prove your absolute loyalty.","hi":"कार्य चुपचाप स्वीकार कर लेना, माता-पिता का चिकित्सा अपॉइंटमेंट रद्द कर देना और अपनी पूर्ण निष्ठा सिद्ध करने के लिए पूरी रात जागकर उसे पूरा करना।"},"2":{"en":"Refuse the task flatly on the spot, telling the director that expecting work outside office hours is toxic and violates your work-life balance.","hi":"उसी समय कार्य स्पष्ट रूप से मना कर देना और निदेशक से कहना कि कार्यालय समय के बाद कार्य करवाना विषाक्त है और कार्य-जीवन संतुलन का उल्लंघन है।"},"3":{"en":"Acknowledge the urgency and propose a staggered timeline to complete data organisation overnight and share final insights by the next morning.","hi":"तात्कालिकता स्वीकार करना और रात भर में डेटा संगठन पूरा करने तथा अगली सुबह तक अंतिम निष्कर्ष साझा करने की चरणबद्ध समय-रेखा प्रस्तावित करना।"},"4":{"en":"Take the file, leave at 5:45 PM for your appointment, and email at midnight explaining it couldn't be done due to a family emergency.","hi":"फ़ाइल लेकर 5:45 बजे अपॉइंटमेंट के लिए निकल जाना और आधी रात को ईमेल करके बताना कि पारिवारिक आपात स्थिति के कारण कार्य नहीं हो सका।"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"An emotionally intelligent reply respects both the director's deadline and the family duty<br>Acknowledging the urgency and offering a staggered timeline shows ownership and keeps both commitments possible ✔<br>Cancelling the appointment harms the parent, refusing flatly damages the working relation and leaving without a plan leaves the director without options<br>Hence acknowledging the urgency and proposing a staggered timeline is the best negotiation<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Acknowledge the urgency and propose a staggered timeline to complete data organisation overnight and share final insights by the next morning.</b>","hi":"भावनात्मक रूप से बुद्धिमान उत्तर निदेशक की समय-सीमा तथा परिवार के कर्तव्य दोनों का सम्मान करता है<br>तात्कालिकता स्वीकार करके चरणबद्ध समय-रेखा देना जिम्मेदारी दर्शाता है और दोनों वचन संभव रखता है ✔<br>अपॉइंटमेंट रद्द करना माता-पिता को हानि पहुँचाता है, स्पष्ट मना करना कार्य-संबंध बिगाड़ता है और बिना योजना निकल जाना निदेशक को विकल्पविहीन छोड़ देता है<br>इसलिए तात्कालिकता स्वीकार करना और चरणबद्ध समय-रेखा प्रस्तावित करना सबसे अच्छी बातचीत है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): तात्कालिकता स्वीकार करना और रात भर में डेटा संगठन पूरा करने तथा अगली सुबह तक अंतिम निष्कर्ष साझा करने की चरणबद्ध समय-रेखा प्रस्तावित करना। है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":17,"local_id":"50017","quid":"Q1000072397","section":"REASONING","topic":"Situational Judgement","question":{"en":"You are a branch manager. Worker Kiran is a single parent whose child is undergoing long-term medical treatments. Out of sympathy, you have overlooked Kiran's chronic lateness for four months. However, the rest of the team has now started complaining because they have to stay late every evening to finish Kiran's pending customer queries. How do you resolve this situation emotionally intelligently? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"आप शाखा प्रबंधक हैं। कर्मचारी Kiran एकल अभिभावक है जिसके बच्चे का लंबे समय से चिकित्सा उपचार चल रहा है। सहानुभूति में आपने चार महीनों से Kiran की लगातार देरी को अनदेखा किया है। अब बाकी टीम शिकायत करने लगी है क्योंकि उन्हें Kiran के लंबित ग्राहक प्रश्न पूरे करने के लिए हर शाम देर तक रुकना पड़ता है। आप इस स्थिति को भावनात्मक रूप से बुद्धिमान तरीके से कैसे सुलझाएँगे? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Tell the complaining team members that they lack empathy and must continue to cover Kiran's shift out of human decency.","hi":"शिकायत करने वाले टीम सदस्यों से कहना कि उनमें सहानुभूति की कमी है और मानवीय संवेदना से उन्हें Kiran की शिफ्ट संभालनी ही होगी।"},"2":{"en":"Privately meet Kiran, acknowledge their stress, note the team impact, and adjust their shift or reassign to a non-live role.","hi":"Kiran से निजी रूप से मिलना, उनका तनाव स्वीकार करना, टीम पर पड़ने वाले प्रभाव को बताना और उनकी शिफ्ट बदलना या गैर-लाइव भूमिका में स्थानांतरित करना।"},"3":{"en":"Give Kiran an immediate formal warning that family issues do not excuse missed office hours.","hi":"Kiran को तुरंत औपचारिक चेतावनी देना कि पारिवारिक समस्याएँ कार्यालय समय चूकने का बहाना नहीं हैं।"},"4":{"en":"Quietly handle Kiran's leftover work yourself every evening to keep everyone happy.","hi":"हर शाम Kiran का बचा हुआ कार्य चुपचाप स्वयं करना ताकि सभी खुश रहें।"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"The manager has to protect both the employee in distress and the fairness of the team<br>Meeting Kiran privately, acknowledging the stress and adjusting the shift or reassigning to a non-live role solves the root cause fairly ✔<br>Blaming the team, giving a formal warning without support and quietly doing the work yourself either hurt people or hide the problem<br>Hence meeting Kiran privately, acknowledging the stress and adjusting the shift is the right step<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Privately meet Kiran, acknowledge their stress, note the team impact, and adjust their shift or reassign to a non-live role.</b>","hi":"प्रबंधक को संकट में कर्मचारी तथा टीम के न्याय दोनों की रक्षा करनी है<br>Kiran से निजी रूप से मिलना, तनाव स्वीकार करना तथा शिफ्ट बदलना या गैर-लाइव भूमिका देना मूल कारण को न्यायपूर्वक सुलझाता है ✔<br>टीम को दोष देना, बिना सहयोग औपचारिक चेतावनी देना और स्वयं चुपचाप कार्य करना — ये या तो लोगों को हानि पहुँचाते हैं या समस्या छिपाते हैं<br>इसलिए Kiran से निजी रूप से मिलना, तनाव स्वीकार करना और शिफ्ट बदलना सही कदम है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): Kiran से निजी रूप से मिलना, उनका तनाव स्वीकार करना, टीम पर पड़ने वाले प्रभाव को बताना और उनकी शिफ्ट बदलना या गैर-लाइव भूमिका में स्थानांतरित करना। है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":18,"local_id":"50018","quid":"Q1000072398","section":"REASONING","topic":"Address/Sentence Matching","question":{"en":"<b>Choose the option which is exactly similar to:</b> Prof. V. K. Malhotra, Dept. of Economics, DU, Delhi-110007 [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"<b>वह विकल्प चुनिए जो ठीक इसके समान है:</b> Prof. V. K. Malhotra, Dept. of Economics, DU, Delhi-110007 [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Prof. V. K. Malhotra, Dept. of Economics, DU, Delhi-110007"},"2":{"en":"Prof V. K. Malhotra, Dept. of Economics, DU, Delhi-110007"},"3":{"en":"Prof V. K. Malhotra, Dept of Economics, DU, Delhi-110007"},"4":{"en":"Prof. V. K. Malhotra, Dept. of Economics, UD, Delhi-110007"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"Option A repeats the given text exactly, with the full stop after Prof., 'Dept. of' and the university as DU ✔<br>Options B and C drop the full stop after Prof. and after Dept., while option D writes UD in place of DU ✘<br>Hence option A is exactly similar to the given text<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Prof. V. K. Malhotra, Dept. of Economics, DU, Delhi-110007.</b>","hi":"विकल्प A दिए गए पाठ को ठीक वैसा ही दोहराता है, Prof. के बाद पूर्ण विराम, 'Dept. of' तथा विश्वविद्यालय DU के रूप में ✔<br>विकल्प B तथा C में Prof. और Dept. के बाद का पूर्ण विराम हट जाता है, जबकि विकल्प D में DU के स्थान पर UD है ✘<br>इसलिए विकल्प A दिए गए पाठ के ठीक समान है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): Prof. V. K. Malhotra, Dept. of Economics, DU, Delhi-110007 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":19,"local_id":"50019","quid":"Q1000072399","section":"REASONING","topic":"Letter/Alphabetical Analogy","question":{"en":"What should come in place of the question mark (?) in the following analogy?<br>KMO : QSU :: EGI : ? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"निम्नलिखित सादृश्य में प्रश्नवाचक चिह्न (?) के स्थान पर क्या आएगा?<br>KMO : QSU :: EGI : ? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"KNO"},"2":{"en":"LNP"},"3":{"en":"KMO"},"4":{"en":"JLM"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"In KMO the letters are 11, 13 and 15, and in QSU they are 17, 19 and 21, so every letter moves six places ahead ✔<br>For EGI the letters are 5, 7 and 9, so adding six gives 11, 13 and 15, that is K, M and O<br>Hence the answer is KMO<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): KMO.</b>","hi":"KMO में अक्षर 11, 13 तथा 15 हैं और QSU में 17, 19 तथा 21, अतः प्रत्येक अक्षर छह स्थान आगे जाता है ✔<br>EGI में अक्षर 5, 7 तथा 9 हैं, अतः छह जोड़ने पर 11, 13 तथा 15 अर्थात् K, M तथा O मिलते हैं<br>इसलिए उत्तर KMO है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): KMO है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":20,"local_id":"50020","quid":"Q1000072400","section":"REASONING","topic":"Mathematical Operations","question":{"en":"Interchange the indicated signs and solve to find the result for both equations (I) and (II) respectively.<br><b>Interchange signs:</b> − and +<br>I. 64 ÷ 8 − 4 × 2 + 10<br>II. 48 × 2 ÷ 8 + 16 − 4 [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"संकेतित चिह्नों को परस्पर बदलकर दोनों समीकरणों (I) तथा (II) का परिणाम ज्ञात कीजिए।<br><b>बदले जाने वाले चिह्न:</b> − तथा +<br>I. 64 ÷ 8 − 4 × 2 + 10<br>II. 48 × 2 ÷ 8 + 16 − 4 [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"8 and 2","hi":"8 तथा 2"},"2":{"en":"6 and 0","hi":"6 तथा 0"},"3":{"en":"6 and 4","hi":"6 तथा 4"},"4":{"en":"10 and 0","hi":"10 तथा 0"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"After interchanging − and + the first equation becomes 64 ÷ 8 + 4 × 2 − 10 = 8 + 8 − 10 = 6 ✔<br>The second equation becomes 48 × 2 ÷ 8 − 16 + 4 = 96 ÷ 8 − 16 + 4 = 12 − 16 + 4 = 0 ✔<br>So the results are 6 and 0<br>Hence the answer is 6 and 0<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 6 and 0.</b>","hi":"− तथा + बदलने पर पहला समीकरण बनता है 64 ÷ 8 + 4 × 2 − 10 = 8 + 8 − 10 = 6 ✔<br>दूसरा समीकरण बनता है 48 × 2 ÷ 8 − 16 + 4 = 96 ÷ 8 − 16 + 4 = 12 − 16 + 4 = 0 ✔<br>अतः परिणाम 6 तथा 0 हैं<br>इसलिए उत्तर 6 तथा 0 है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 6 तथा 0 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":21,"local_id":"50021","quid":"Q1000072401","section":"REASONING","topic":"Eligibility","question":{"en":"Read the given conditions carefully and determine the appropriate outcome for the case provided. If any exception applies, identify the authority to whom the case should be referred.<br><b>Criteria for Advanced Research Grant Allocation:</b><br>(i) Must have published 3+ papers.<br>(ii) Must be currently enrolled in a PhD program.<br><b>Exceptions:</b><br><b>Exception (A):</b> If the candidate has published 5+ papers but is not enrolled in a PhD, refer the case to the Grant Committee.<br><b>Exception (B):</b> If the candidate meets criteria (i) and (ii) but has a project scope exceeding the budget limit, refer the case to the Finance Oversight Board.<br><b>Case:</b> The candidate has published 6 papers and is not enrolled in a PhD program. [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"दी गई शर्तें ध्यान से पढ़िए और दिए गए मामले के लिए उपयुक्त परिणाम निर्धारित कीजिए। यदि कोई अपवाद लागू हो तो वह प्राधिकरण पहचानिए जिसे मामला भेजा जाना चाहिए।<br><b>उन्नत अनुसंधान अनुदान आवंटन के मानदंड:</b><br>(i) 3+ शोध-पत्र प्रकाशित होने चाहिए।<br>(ii) वर्तमान में PhD कार्यक्रम में नामांकित होना चाहिए।<br><b>अपवाद:</b><br><b>अपवाद (A):</b> यदि उम्मीदवार ने 5+ शोध-पत्र प्रकाशित किए हैं परंतु PhD में नामांकित नहीं है, तो मामला Grant Committee को भेजें।<br><b>अपवाद (B):</b> यदि उम्मीदवार मानदंड (i) तथा (ii) पूरा करता हो परंतु परियोजना का दायरा बजट सीमा से अधिक हो, तो मामला Finance Oversight Board को भेजें।<br><b>मामला:</b> उम्मीदवार ने 6 शोध-पत्र प्रकाशित किए हैं और PhD कार्यक्रम में नामांकित नहीं है। [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Grant to be approved","hi":"अनुदान स्वीकृत किया जाए"},"2":{"en":"Grant application to be rejected","hi":"अनुदान आवेदन अस्वीकार किया जाए"},"3":{"en":"Case to be referred to the Grant Committee","hi":"मामला Grant Committee को भेजा जाए"},"4":{"en":"Case to be referred to the Finance Oversight Board","hi":"मामला Finance Oversight Board को भेजा जाए"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"The candidate has published 6 papers, which satisfies condition (i), but is not enrolled in a PhD, so condition (ii) fails<br>Since the candidate has published more than 5 papers without PhD enrolment, Exception (A) applies ✔<br>Exception (B) needs both basic criteria to be met, which is not the case here<br>Hence the case is to be referred to the Grant Committee<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Case to be referred to the Grant Committee.</b>","hi":"उम्मीदवार ने 6 शोध-पत्र प्रकाशित किए हैं, जिससे शर्त (i) पूरी होती है, परंतु वह PhD में नामांकित नहीं है, अतः शर्त (ii) पूरी नहीं होती<br>चूँकि उम्मीदवार ने PhD नामांकन के बिना 5 से अधिक शोध-पत्र प्रकाशित किए हैं, अपवाद (A) लागू होता है ✔<br>अपवाद (B) के लिए दोनों मूल मानदंड पूरे होने चाहिए, जो यहाँ नहीं हैं<br>इसलिए मामला Grant Committee को भेजा जाए<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): मामला Grant Committee को भेजा जाए है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":22,"local_id":"50022","quid":"Q1000072402","section":"REASONING","topic":"Situational Judgement","question":{"en":"Your company has a policy prohibiting the use of office resources for personal projects. You have a small, urgent personal task that would take 10 minutes and requires a company printer. What do you do? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"आपकी कंपनी की नीति व्यक्तिगत कार्यों के लिए कार्यालय के संसाधनों के उपयोग को प्रतिबंधित करती है। आपका एक छोटा, तात्कालिक व्यक्तिगत कार्य है जिसमें 10 मिनट लगेंगे और कंपनी के प्रिंटर की आवश्यकता होगी। आप क्या करेंगे? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Use the printer quickly, as it is a minor task.","hi":"चूँकि कार्य छोटा है, प्रिंटर का शीघ्र उपयोग कर लेना।"},"2":{"en":"Ask for special permission from your manager for this one time.","hi":"इस एक बार के लिए प्रबंधक से विशेष अनुमति माँगना।"},"3":{"en":"Seek an alternative solution outside the office to comply with policy.","hi":"नीति का पालन करने के लिए कार्यालय के बाहर वैकल्पिक समाधान खोजना।"},"4":{"en":"Use the printer but pay the company for the paper and ink used.","hi":"प्रिंटर का उपयोग करना परंतु कागज़ और स्याही का भुगतान कंपनी को करना।"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"The policy is clear, so the personal task must be completed without using office resources<br>Finding an alternative solution outside the office respects the rule completely ✔<br>Using the printer quickly still breaks the rule, one-time permission depends on the manager, and paying for paper does not make the use of office resources permissible<br>Hence seeking an alternative solution outside the office is the right step<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Seek an alternative solution outside the office to comply with policy.</b>","hi":"नीति स्पष्ट है, अतः व्यक्तिगत कार्य कार्यालय के संसाधनों का उपयोग किए बिना पूरा होना चाहिए<br>कार्यालय के बाहर वैकल्पिक समाधान खोजना नियम का पूरी तरह पालन करता है ✔<br>जल्दी प्रिंटर का उपयोग करना भी नियम तोड़ता है, एक बार की अनुमति प्रबंधक पर निर्भर है, और कागज़ का भुगतान करने से कार्यालय संसाधन का उपयोग वैध नहीं हो जाता<br>इसलिए कार्यालय के बाहर वैकल्पिक समाधान खोजना सही कदम है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): नीति का पालन करने के लिए कार्यालय के बाहर वैकल्पिक समाधान खोजना। है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":23,"local_id":"50023","quid":"Q1000072403","section":"REASONING","topic":"Statement & Conclusion","question":{"en":"Read the statement carefully and assume it to be true. Then examine the two conclusions given below it and decide which conclusion(s), if any, logically follow from the statement.<br><b>Statement:</b><br>After analysing customer feedback, a smartphone manufacturer decided to extend software support for its premium devices from three years to five years.<br><b>Conclusions:</b><br>I. The manufacturer believes longer software support may increase customer satisfaction.<br>II. All customers purchase smartphones primarily because of software support duration. [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"कथन को ध्यान से पढ़िए और उसे सत्य मानिए। फिर उसके नीचे दिए दो निष्कर्षों की जाँच कीजिए और निर्णय कीजिए कि कौन-सा/से निष्कर्ष कथन से तार्किक रूप से निकलता/निकलते हैं।<br><b>कथन:</b><br>ग्राहक प्रतिक्रिया का विश्लेषण करने के बाद एक स्मार्टफोन निर्माता ने अपने प्रीमियम उपकरणों के लिए सॉफ्टवेयर सहायता तीन वर्ष से बढ़ाकर पाँच वर्ष करने का निर्णय लिया।<br><b>निष्कर्ष:</b><br>I. निर्माता मानता है कि लंबी सॉफ्टवेयर सहायता ग्राहक संतुष्टि बढ़ा सकती है।<br>II. सभी ग्राहक मुख्य रूप से सॉफ्टवेयर सहायता की अवधि के कारण स्मार्टफोन खरीदते हैं। [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only conclusion I follows","hi":"केवल निष्कर्ष I निकलता है"},"2":{"en":"Only conclusion II follows","hi":"केवल निष्कर्ष II निकलता है"},"3":{"en":"Neither conclusion I nor conclusion II follows","hi":"न तो निष्कर्ष I और न ही निष्कर्ष II निकलता है"},"4":{"en":"Both conclusions I and II follow","hi":"निष्कर्ष I और II दोनों निकलते हैं"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"The decision was taken after studying customer feedback, so the company expects the longer support to please customers, which is conclusion I ✔<br>The word 'all' in conclusion II is far too wide, because many other features decide a purchase ✘<br>Hence only conclusion I follows<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Only conclusion I follows.</b>","hi":"निर्णय ग्राहक प्रतिक्रिया पढ़ने के बाद लिया गया, अतः कंपनी अपेक्षा करती है कि लंबी सहायता ग्राहकों को संतुष्ट करेगी, जो निष्कर्ष I है ✔<br>निष्कर्ष II में 'सभी' शब्द अत्यधिक व्यापक है, क्योंकि खरीद अनेक अन्य विशेषताओं से तय होती है ✘<br>इसलिए केवल निष्कर्ष I निकलता है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): केवल निष्कर्ष I निकलता है है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":24,"local_id":"50024","quid":"Q1000072404","section":"REASONING","topic":"Statement, Assumption & Argument","question":{"en":"Read the given statement carefully and the following assumptions based on it. Decide which of the assumptions are implicit in the statement.<br><b>Statement:</b><br>To reduce traffic congestion during peak hours, the municipal corporation should introduce a congestion charge on all private vehicles entering the city centre.<br><b>Assumptions:</b><br>I. Charging a fee for entering the city centre will discourage many private vehicle owners from using that route.<br>II. Heavy traffic congestion adversely affects the smooth functioning of the city. [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"दिया गया कथन तथा उस पर आधारित अवधारणाएँ ध्यान से पढ़िए और निर्णय कीजिए कि कौन-सी अवधारणाएँ कथन में निहित हैं।<br><b>कथन:</b><br>व्यस्त समय में यातायात भीड़ कम करने के लिए नगर निगम को शहर के केंद्र में प्रवेश करने वाले सभी निजी वाहनों पर भीड़-शुल्क लगाना चाहिए।<br><b>अवधारणाएँ:</b><br>I. शहर के केंद्र में प्रवेश पर शुल्क लेने से अनेक निजी वाहन स्वामी उस मार्ग का उपयोग करना छोड़ देंगे।<br>II. अत्यधिक यातायात भीड़ शहर के सुचारु संचालन पर बुरा प्रभाव डालती है। [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Only Assumption I is implicit","hi":"केवल अवधारणा I निहित है"},"2":{"en":"Both Assumptions I and II are implicit","hi":"अवधारणा I और II दोनों निहित हैं"},"3":{"en":"Only Assumption II is implicit","hi":"केवल अवधारणा II निहित है"},"4":{"en":"Neither Assumption I nor II is implicit","hi":"न तो अवधारणा I और न ही II निहित है"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"A congestion charge is proposed only because the fee is expected to keep many private vehicles away, so assumption I is implicit ✔<br>The proposal exists to cut peak-hour congestion, which means congestion is taken to be a real problem for the city, so assumption II is also implicit ✔<br>Hence both assumptions I and II are implicit<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Both Assumptions I and II are implicit.</b>","hi":"भीड़-शुल्क इसलिए प्रस्तावित है क्योंकि शुल्क से अनेक निजी वाहन दूर रहेंगे, अतः अवधारणा I निहित है ✔<br>यह प्रस्ताव व्यस्त समय की भीड़ घटाने के लिए है, अर्थात् भीड़ को शहर की वास्तविक समस्या माना गया है, अतः अवधारणा II भी निहित है ✔<br>इसलिए अवधारणा I और II दोनों निहित हैं<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): अवधारणा I और II दोनों निहित हैं है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":25,"local_id":"50025","quid":"Q1000072405","section":"REASONING","topic":"Word Analogy","question":{"en":"Select the option that is related to the third word in the same way as the second word is related to the first word. (The words must be considered as meaningful English words and must not be related to each other based on the number of letters/number of consonants/vowels in the word.)<br>Ornithology : Birds :: Ichthyology : ? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"वह विकल्प चुनिए जो तीसरे शब्द से उसी प्रकार संबंधित है जिस प्रकार दूसरा शब्द पहले शब्द से संबंधित है। (शब्द अर्थपूर्ण अंग्रेज़ी शब्द माने जाने चाहिए और अक्षरों/व्यंजनों/स्वरों की संख्या के आधार पर संबंधित नहीं होने चाहिए।)<br>Ornithology : Birds :: Ichthyology : ? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Reptiles","hi":"सरीसृप"},"2":{"en":"Amphibians","hi":"उभयचर"},"3":{"en":"Fish","hi":"मछली"},"4":{"en":"Insects","hi":"कीट"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Ornithology is the study of birds<br>In the same way Ichthyology is the study of fish ✔<br>Reptiles, amphibians and insects are studied in other branches of zoology<br>Hence the answer is Fish<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Fish.</b>","hi":"Ornithology पक्षियों के अध्ययन का विषय है<br>उसी प्रकार Ichthyology मछलियों के अध्ययन का विषय है ✔<br>सरीसृप, उभयचर तथा कीट प्राणि-विज्ञान की अन्य शाखाओं में पढ़े जाते हैं<br>इसलिए उत्तर Fish है<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): मछली है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false}]},"GK":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":26,"local_id":"50026","quid":"Q1000072406","section":"GK","topic":"Medieval History: Delhi Sultanate","question":{"en":"Who among the following did NOT ascend the throne of the Delhi Sultanate? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"निम्नलिखित में से कौन दिल्ली सल्तनत के सिंहासन पर नहीं बैठा? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Razia Sultana","hi":"रज़िया सुल्तान"},"2":{"en":"Khizr Khan","hi":"ख़िज़्र ख़ान"},"3":{"en":"Malik Kafur","hi":"मलिक काफ़ूर"},"4":{"en":"Alauddin Khalji","hi":"अलाउद्दीन ख़िलजी"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Malik Kafur</b><br><b><u>Malik Kafur</u></b> was Alauddin Khalji's general. After Alauddin's death (1316) he ruled briefly as <b>regent</b> by placing the child <b>Shihabuddin Umar</b> on the throne, but never became Sultan himself; he was soon killed.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Malik Kafur led Alauddin's campaigns to the <b>Deccan and South India</b> (Devagiri, Warangal, Dwarasamudra, Madurai).<br>• <b>Razia Sultana</b> (1236–40) – first and only woman ruler of the Delhi Sultanate.<br>• <b>Khizr Khan</b> founded the <b>Sayyid dynasty</b> in <b>1414</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – मलिक काफ़ूर</b><br><b><u>मलिक काफ़ूर</u></b> अलाउद्दीन ख़िलजी का सेनापति था। अलाउद्दीन की मृत्यु (1316) के बाद उसने बालक <b>शिहाबुद्दीन उमर</b> को गद्दी पर बैठाकर कुछ समय <b>संरक्षक (Regent)</b> के रूप में शासन किया, परंतु स्वयं कभी सुल्तान नहीं बना; शीघ्र ही उसकी हत्या कर दी गई।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• मलिक काफ़ूर ने अलाउद्दीन के <b>दक्कन और दक्षिण भारत</b> अभियानों (देवगिरि, वारंगल, द्वारसमुद्र, मदुरै) का नेतृत्व किया।<br>• <b>रज़िया सुल्तान</b> (1236–40) – दिल्ली सल्तनत की पहली और एकमात्र महिला शासक।<br>• <b>ख़िज़्र ख़ान</b> ने <b>1414</b> में <b>सैयद वंश</b> की स्थापना की।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":27,"local_id":"50027","quid":"Q1000072407","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: International Organisations","question":{"en":"Where was the 1<sup>st</sup> BRICS summit held? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"पहला ब्रिक्स शिखर सम्मेलन कहाँ आयोजित हुआ था? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"USA","hi":"अमेरिका"},"2":{"en":"China","hi":"चीन"},"3":{"en":"France","hi":"फ्रांस"},"4":{"en":"Russia","hi":"रूस"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (4) – Russia</b><br>The first summit of BRIC was held at <b>Yekaterinburg</b>, <b><u>Russia</u></b>, on <b>16 June 2009</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• South Africa joined in <b>2010</b>, and its first summit as a member was at <b>Sanya, China (2011)</b>.<br>• India hosted BRICS summits in <b>2012, 2016 and 2021</b>, and chairs BRICS in <b>2026</b>.<br>• The <b>New Development Bank</b> (HQ Shanghai) was agreed at the <b>Fortaleza summit (2014)</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (4) – रूस</b><br>BRIC का पहला शिखर सम्मेलन <b>16 जून 2009</b> को <b><u>रूस</u></b> के <b>येकातेरिनबर्ग</b> में हुआ।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• दक्षिण अफ्रीका <b>2010</b> में शामिल हुआ और सदस्य के रूप में उसका पहला शिखर सम्मेलन <b>सान्या, चीन (2011)</b> में हुआ।<br>• भारत ने <b>2012, 2016 और 2021</b> में ब्रिक्स शिखर सम्मेलनों की मेज़बानी की और <b>2026</b> में ब्रिक्स की अध्यक्षता कर रहा है।<br>• <b>न्यू डेवलपमेंट बैंक</b> (मुख्यालय शंघाई) पर <b>फ़ोर्टालेज़ा शिखर सम्मेलन (2014)</b> में सहमति बनी।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":28,"local_id":"50028","quid":"Q1000072408","section":"GK","topic":"Current Affairs: International News","question":{"en":"The IMEC (India-Middle East-Europe Economic Corridor) project is designed to increase _________ between the participating nations. [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"IMEC (भारत-मध्य पूर्व-यूरोप आर्थिक गलियारा) परियोजना भागीदार देशों के बीच _________ बढ़ाने के लिए बनाई गई है। [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"economic integration","hi":"आर्थिक एकीकरण"},"2":{"en":"military alliances","hi":"सैन्य गठबंधन"},"3":{"en":"population exchanges","hi":"जनसंख्या आदान-प्रदान"},"4":{"en":"cultural uniformity","hi":"सांस्कृतिक एकरूपता"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – economic integration</b><br>IMEC aims to boost <b><u>economic integration</u></b> between Asia, the Arabian Gulf and Europe through rail and shipping links, energy pipelines and digital connectivity.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The IMEC MoU was signed on the sidelines of the <b>G20 New Delhi Summit (September 2023)</b>.<br>• Signatories: <b>India, USA, Saudi Arabia, UAE, EU, France, Germany and Italy</b>.<br>• It has an <b>Eastern Corridor</b> (India–Gulf) and a <b>Northern Corridor</b> (Gulf–Europe).","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – आर्थिक एकीकरण</b><br>IMEC का उद्देश्य रेल और जहाज़रानी संपर्क, ऊर्जा पाइपलाइनों और डिजिटल कनेक्टिविटी के माध्यम से एशिया, अरब खाड़ी और यूरोप के बीच <b><u>आर्थिक एकीकरण</u></b> बढ़ाना है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• IMEC पर MoU <b>G20 नई दिल्ली शिखर सम्मेलन (सितंबर 2023)</b> के दौरान हस्ताक्षरित हुआ।<br>• हस्ताक्षरकर्ता: <b>भारत, अमेरिका, सऊदी अरब, UAE, यूरोपीय संघ, फ्रांस, जर्मनी और इटली</b>।<br>• इसमें <b>पूर्वी गलियारा</b> (भारत–खाड़ी) और <b>उत्तरी गलियारा</b> (खाड़ी–यूरोप) है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":29,"local_id":"50029","quid":"Q1000072409","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Sports(Static & Current)","question":{"en":"With which sport is the term \"googly\" traditionally associated? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"\"गुगली\" शब्द पारंपरिक रूप से किस खेल से संबंधित है? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Hockey","hi":"हॉकी"},"2":{"en":"Cricket","hi":"क्रिकेट"},"3":{"en":"Football","hi":"फ़ुटबॉल"},"4":{"en":"Kabaddi","hi":"कबड्डी"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Cricket</b><br>A <b>googly</b> is a deceptive delivery in <b><u>cricket</u></b> bowled by a leg-spinner that turns the opposite way (from off to leg for a right-handed batter).<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The googly was invented by England's <b>Bernard Bosanquet</b>; it is also called the <b>\"wrong'un\"</b>.<br>• Other cricket terms: <b>doosra, yorker, chinaman, bouncer, LBW</b>.<br>• Hockey terms: <b>penalty corner, bully, dribble</b>; Kabaddi terms: <b>raid, cant, lona</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – क्रिकेट</b><br><b>गुगली</b> <b><u>क्रिकेट</u></b> में लेग-स्पिनर द्वारा फेंकी जाने वाली भ्रामक गेंद है, जो विपरीत दिशा में (दाएँ हाथ के बल्लेबाज़ के लिए ऑफ से लेग की ओर) घूमती है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• गुगली का आविष्कार इंग्लैंड के <b>बर्नार्ड बोसांक्वेट</b> ने किया; इसे <b>\"रॉन्ग'अन\"</b> भी कहते हैं।<br>• क्रिकेट के अन्य शब्द: <b>दूसरा, यॉर्कर, चाइनामैन, बाउंसर, LBW</b>।<br>• हॉकी के शब्द: <b>पेनल्टी कॉर्नर, बुली, ड्रिबल</b>; कबड्डी के शब्द: <b>रेड, कैंट, लोना</b>।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":30,"local_id":"50030","quid":"Q1000072410","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Books and Authors","question":{"en":"Which Indian English novel, written in 1956, is often cited as the first modern English novel from India? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"1956 में लिखा गया कौन-सा भारतीय अंग्रेज़ी उपन्यास प्रायः भारत का पहला आधुनिक अंग्रेज़ी उपन्यास कहा जाता है? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Untouchable","hi":"अनटचेबल"},"2":{"en":"Train to Pakistan","hi":"ट्रेन टू पाकिस्तान"},"3":{"en":"The Serpent and the Rope","hi":"द सर्पेंट एंड द रोप"},"4":{"en":"The Guide","hi":"द गाइड"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Train to Pakistan</b><br><b>Train to Pakistan</b> by <b>Khushwant Singh</b>, published in <b>1956</b>, is the Indian English novel usually cited as the first modern English novel from India; it is set in the fictional village of <b>Mano Majra</b> on the India-Pakistan border during the Partition of 1947.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>Mulk Raj Anand’s Untouchable (1935)</b> came earlier but is read as 1930s social realism rather than the start of the modern novel.<br>• <b>Raja Rao’s The Serpent and the Rope (1960)</b> and <b>R. K. Narayan’s The Guide (1958)</b> belong to the same post-Independence wave.<br>• Khushwant Singh also wrote <b>A History of the Sikhs</b> and the short-story collection <b>The Mark of Vishnu</b>.<br>• The novel won the <b>Grove Press Award</b> and was later made into a film of the same name.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – ट्रेन टू पाकिस्तान</b><br><b>खुशवंत सिंह</b> का <b>1956</b> में प्रकाशित <b>ट्रेन टू पाकिस्तान</b> वह भारतीय अंग्रेज़ी उपन्यास है जिसे सामान्यतः भारत का पहला आधुनिक अंग्रेज़ी उपन्यास कहा जाता है; इसकी कथा 1947 के विभाजन के समय भारत-पाकिस्तान सीमा पर स्थित काल्पनिक गाँव <b>मनो माजरा</b> में घटती है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>मुल्क राज आनंद का अनटचेबल (1935)</b> पहले आया, परंतु उसे आधुनिक उपन्यास का आरंभ नहीं, 1930 के दशक का सामाजिक यथार्थवाद माना जाता है।<br>• <b>राजा राव का द सर्पेंट एंड द रोप (1960)</b> तथा <b>आर. के. नारायण का द गाइड (1958)</b> स्वतंत्रता के बाद की उसी कथा-धारा के उपन्यास हैं।<br>• खुशवंत सिंह ने <b>अ हिस्ट्री ऑफ द सिख्स</b> तथा कहानी-संग्रह <b>द मार्क ऑफ विष्णु</b> भी लिखा।<br>• इस उपन्यास को <b>ग्रोव प्रेस पुरस्कार</b> मिला और बाद में इसी नाम से फिल्म बनी।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":31,"local_id":"50031","quid":"Q1000072411","section":"GK","topic":"Economics: Five Year Plan and Industrial Policy Resolution","question":{"en":"According to the Seventh Five-Year Plan (1985-1990), why was the railway system considered vital to the Indian economy? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"सातवीं पंचवर्षीय योजना (1985-1990) के अनुसार रेलवे प्रणाली को भारतीय अर्थव्यवस्था के लिए महत्वपूर्ण क्यों माना गया? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"It was the only mode of transport available","hi":"यह उपलब्ध परिवहन का एकमात्र साधन था"},"2":{"en":"It reduced the need for road transport","hi":"इससे सड़क परिवहन की आवश्यकता कम हुई"},"3":{"en":"It primarily supported urban development","hi":"यह मुख्य रूप से शहरी विकास में सहायक था"},"4":{"en":"It was the backbone of the country’s transport infrastructure","hi":"यह देश की परिवहन अवसंरचना की रीढ़ थी"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (4) – It was the backbone of the country’s transport infrastructure</b><br>The Seventh Plan described the Indian Railways as the <b><u>backbone of the country's transport infrastructure</u></b>, carrying the bulk of long-distance freight (coal, steel, foodgrains) and passengers.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The Seventh Plan focused on <b>\"Food, Work and Productivity\"</b>; it achieved growth of about <b>6%</b>.<br>• Indian Railways is the <b>fourth largest</b> rail network in the world; first train ran on <b>16 April 1853</b> (Bori Bunder–Thane).<br>• Indian Railways is divided into <b>17–18 zones</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (4) – यह देश की परिवहन अवसंरचना की रीढ़ थी</b><br>सातवीं योजना ने भारतीय रेलवे को <b><u>देश की परिवहन अवसंरचना की रीढ़</u></b> बताया, जो लंबी दूरी के अधिकांश माल (कोयला, इस्पात, खाद्यान्न) और यात्रियों का परिवहन करती है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• सातवीं योजना का फोकस <b>\"भोजन, काम और उत्पादकता\"</b> था; इसने लगभग <b>6%</b> वृद्धि प्राप्त की।<br>• भारतीय रेलवे विश्व का <b>चौथा सबसे बड़ा</b> रेल नेटवर्क है; पहली ट्रेन <b>16 अप्रैल 1853</b> (बोरी बंदर–ठाणे) को चली।<br>• भारतीय रेलवे <b>17–18 ज़ोन</b> में विभाजित है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":32,"local_id":"50032","quid":"Q1000072412","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Sports(Static & Current)","question":{"en":"In Kabaddi, what is the maximum number of substitutions per team? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"कबड्डी में प्रति टीम अधिकतम कितने प्रतिस्थापन (substitutions) होते हैं? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"3"},"2":{"en":"4"},"3":{"en":"5"},"4":{"en":"6"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – 5</b><br>As per Kabaddi rules, a team has <b>12 players</b> – 7 on court and 5 substitutes – and a maximum of <b><u>5 substitutions</u></b> can be made during a match.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• A substituted (out) player cannot be replaced; substitution is allowed only with the referee's permission during time-out or interval.<br>• Kabaddi is played on a court of <b>13 m × 10 m</b> (men).<br>• <b>Pro Kabaddi League</b> started in <b>2014</b>; India has won all Kabaddi World Cups.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – 5</b><br>कबड्डी नियमों के अनुसार एक टीम में <b>12 खिलाड़ी</b> होते हैं – 7 कोर्ट पर और 5 स्थानापन्न – और मैच के दौरान अधिकतम <b><u>5 प्रतिस्थापन</u></b> किए जा सकते हैं।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• बाहर (आउट) खिलाड़ी को प्रतिस्थापित नहीं किया जा सकता; प्रतिस्थापन केवल टाइम-आउट या मध्यांतर में रेफरी की अनुमति से होता है।<br>• कबड्डी <b>13 m × 10 m</b> (पुरुष) के कोर्ट पर खेली जाती है।<br>• <b>प्रो कबड्डी लीग</b> <b>2014</b> में शुरू हुई; भारत ने सभी कबड्डी विश्व कप जीते हैं।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":33,"local_id":"50033","quid":"Q1000072413","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Folk Dances and Festivals","question":{"en":"The Pushkar Mela, known for its camel trade and vibrant cultural events is celebrated in which state of India? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"ऊँटों के व्यापार और जीवंत सांस्कृतिक कार्यक्रमों के लिए प्रसिद्ध पुष्कर मेला भारत के किस राज्य में मनाया जाता है? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Rajasthan","hi":"राजस्थान"},"2":{"en":"Uttar Pradesh","hi":"उत्तर प्रदेश"},"3":{"en":"Gujarat","hi":"गुजरात"},"4":{"en":"Maharashtra","hi":"महाराष्ट्र"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Rajasthan</b><br>The <b>Pushkar Mela</b> is held in <b>Pushkar (Ajmer district)</b>, <b><u>Rajasthan</u></b>, in the month of <b>Kartik</b> (October–November), ending on Kartik Purnima. It is one of the world's largest camel fairs.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Pushkar has one of the very few <b>Brahma temples</b> in the world.<br>• Pilgrims bathe in the holy <b>Pushkar Lake</b> on Kartik Purnima.<br>• Other Rajasthan fairs: <b>Nagaur cattle fair, Desert Festival (Jaisalmer)</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – राजस्थान</b><br><b>पुष्कर मेला</b> <b><u>राजस्थान</u></b> के <b>पुष्कर (अजमेर ज़िला)</b> में <b>कार्तिक</b> मास (अक्टूबर–नवंबर) में लगता है और कार्तिक पूर्णिमा को समाप्त होता है। यह विश्व के सबसे बड़े ऊँट मेलों में से एक है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• पुष्कर में विश्व के गिने-चुने <b>ब्रह्मा मंदिरों</b> में से एक है।<br>• तीर्थयात्री कार्तिक पूर्णिमा को पवित्र <b>पुष्कर झील</b> में स्नान करते हैं।<br>• राजस्थान के अन्य मेले: <b>नागौर पशु मेला, मरु महोत्सव (जैसलमेर)</b>।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":34,"local_id":"50034","quid":"Q1000072414","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: New Criminal Laws 2023","question":{"en":"What does the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita (BNS), 2023 propose regarding the role of digital evidence in criminal cases? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"भारतीय न्याय संहिता (BNS), 2023 आपराधिक मामलों में डिजिटल साक्ष्य की भूमिका के संबंध में क्या प्रस्तावित करती है? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Digital evidence can only be used if it is manually compiled","hi":"डिजिटल साक्ष्य का उपयोग तभी हो सकता है जब उसे हाथ से संकलित किया गया हो"},"2":{"en":"Digital evidence is not admissible in court without physical copies","hi":"भौतिक प्रतियों के बिना डिजिटल साक्ष्य न्यायालय में ग्राह्य नहीं है"},"3":{"en":"Digital evidence must be verified and authenticated for it to be used in court","hi":"न्यायालय में उपयोग के लिए डिजिटल साक्ष्य का सत्यापन और प्रमाणीकरण आवश्यक है"},"4":{"en":"All digital evidence is automatically accepted in legal proceedings","hi":"सभी डिजिटल साक्ष्य स्वतः कानूनी कार्यवाही में स्वीकार कर लिए जाते हैं"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Digital evidence must be verified and authenticated for it to be used in court</b><br>Under the new criminal laws, electronic and digital records are recognised as evidence, but they <b><u>must be verified and authenticated</u></b> (with a certificate, hash value etc.) before the court relies on them.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Admissibility of electronic records is governed by <b>Section 63 of the Bharatiya Sakshya Adhiniyam</b> (old Sec. 65B).<br>• BNS defines \"document\" to include <b>electronic and digital records</b>.<br>• The three new laws – <b>BNS, BNSS, BSA</b> – came into force on <b>1 July 2024</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – न्यायालय में उपयोग के लिए डिजिटल साक्ष्य का सत्यापन और प्रमाणीकरण आवश्यक है</b><br>नए आपराधिक कानूनों के तहत इलेक्ट्रॉनिक और डिजिटल अभिलेख साक्ष्य के रूप में मान्य हैं, परंतु न्यायालय द्वारा उन पर भरोसा करने से पहले उनका (प्रमाणपत्र, हैश मान आदि से) <b><u>सत्यापन और प्रमाणीकरण आवश्यक</u></b> है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• इलेक्ट्रॉनिक अभिलेखों की ग्राह्यता <b>भारतीय साक्ष्य अधिनियम की धारा 63</b> (पुरानी धारा 65B) से शासित है।<br>• BNS \"दस्तावेज़\" की परिभाषा में <b>इलेक्ट्रॉनिक और डिजिटल अभिलेख</b> शामिल करती है।<br>• तीनों नए कानून – <b>BNS, BNSS, BSA</b> – <b>1 जुलाई 2024</b> से लागू हुए।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":35,"local_id":"50035","quid":"Q1000072415","section":"GK","topic":"Modern History: Quit India Movement","question":{"en":"During the Indian freedom struggle, who organized the ‘Secret Congress Radio’ that broadcasted recorded messages from Gandhiji? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"भारतीय स्वतंत्रता संग्राम के दौरान गांधीजी के रिकॉर्ड किए गए संदेशों का प्रसारण करने वाला ‘गुप्त कांग्रेस रेडियो’ किसने संचालित किया? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Usha Mehta","hi":"उषा मेहता"},"2":{"en":"Alluri Sitarama Raju","hi":"अल्लूरी सीताराम राजू"},"3":{"en":"Kanuri Lakshmibai","hi":"कनुरी लक्ष्मीबाई"},"4":{"en":"Oruganti Mahalakshmamma","hi":"ओरुगंती महालक्ष्मम्मा"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Usha Mehta</b><br><b><u>Usha Mehta</u></b> ran the underground <b>Congress Radio</b> from Bombay during the <b>Quit India Movement (1942)</b>; it began broadcasting on <b>14 August 1942</b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• She was arrested in November 1942 and received the <b>Padma Vibhushan</b> in <b>1998</b>.<br>• <b>Alluri Sitarama Raju</b> led the <b>Rampa Rebellion (1922–24)</b> in Andhra.<br>• Other Quit India figures: <b>Aruna Asaf Ali</b> (hoisted flag at Gowalia Tank), <b>Jayaprakash Narayan, Ram Manohar Lohia</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – उषा मेहता</b><br><b><u>उषा मेहता</u></b> ने <b>भारत छोड़ो आंदोलन (1942)</b> के दौरान बंबई से भूमिगत <b>कांग्रेस रेडियो</b> चलाया; इसका प्रसारण <b>14 अगस्त 1942</b> को शुरू हुआ।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• उन्हें नवंबर 1942 में गिरफ़्तार किया गया और <b>1998</b> में <b>पद्म विभूषण</b> मिला।<br>• <b>अल्लूरी सीताराम राजू</b> ने आंध्र में <b>रम्पा विद्रोह (1922–24)</b> का नेतृत्व किया।<br>• भारत छोड़ो के अन्य नेता: <b>अरुणा आसफ़ अली</b> (गोवालिया टैंक पर ध्वज फहराया), <b>जयप्रकाश नारायण, राम मनोहर लोहिया</b>।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":36,"local_id":"50036","quid":"Q1000072416","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Books and Authors","question":{"en":"Rabindranath Tagore is the author of national anthems of India and which other country? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"रवींद्रनाथ टैगोर भारत और किस अन्य देश के राष्ट्रगान के रचयिता हैं? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Nepal","hi":"नेपाल"},"2":{"en":"Sri lanka","hi":"श्रीलंका"},"3":{"en":"Bangladesh","hi":"बांग्लादेश"},"4":{"en":"Bhutan","hi":"भूटान"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Bangladesh</b><br>Tagore wrote <b>\"Jana Gana Mana\"</b> (India) and <b>\"Amar Shonar Bangla\"</b>, the national anthem of <b><u>Bangladesh</u></b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• \"Jana Gana Mana\" was first sung at the <b>Calcutta session of INC</b> on <b>27 December 1911</b>; adopted on <b>24 January 1950</b>.<br>• Sri Lanka's anthem <b>\"Sri Lanka Matha\"</b> was written by <b>Ananda Samarakoon</b>, a student of Tagore (inspired by him).<br>• Tagore won the <b>Nobel Prize in Literature (1913)</b> for <b>Gitanjali</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – बांग्लादेश</b><br>टैगोर ने <b>\"जन गण मन\"</b> (भारत) और <b><u>बांग्लादेश</u></b> का राष्ट्रगान <b>\"आमार सोनार बांग्ला\"</b> लिखा।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• \"जन गण मन\" पहली बार <b>27 दिसंबर 1911</b> को <b>कांग्रेस के कलकत्ता अधिवेशन</b> में गाया गया; <b>24 जनवरी 1950</b> को अपनाया गया।<br>• श्रीलंका का राष्ट्रगान <b>\"श्रीलंका माता\"</b> टैगोर के शिष्य <b>आनंद समरकून</b> ने लिखा (उनसे प्रेरित)।<br>• टैगोर ने <b>गीतांजलि</b> के लिए <b>साहित्य का नोबेल पुरस्कार (1913)</b> जीता।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":37,"local_id":"50037","quid":"Q1000072417","section":"GK","topic":"Geography: Earth's Interior and Plate Tectonics & Latitude and Longitude","question":{"en":"The States of Jammu and Kashmir, Himachal Pradesh and Uttaranchal are highly vulnerable to earthquakes because:<br>1. The Indian plate is slowly moving towards the north and north-eastern direction, which is obstructed by the Eurasian plate.<br>2. Most of the active volcanoes in India lie in the northern region of the country, which is frequently affected by magma and seismic movements.<br>Which of the above statements is/are CORRECT? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"जम्मू और कश्मीर, हिमाचल प्रदेश और उत्तरांचल राज्य भूकंपों के प्रति अत्यधिक संवेदनशील हैं क्योंकि:<br>1. भारतीय प्लेट धीरे-धीरे उत्तर और उत्तर-पूर्व दिशा में खिसक रही है, जिसे यूरेशियाई प्लेट द्वारा रोका जाता है।<br>2. भारत के अधिकांश सक्रिय ज्वालामुखी देश के उत्तरी क्षेत्र में स्थित हैं, जो मैग्मा और भूकंपीय गतिविधियों से बार-बार प्रभावित होता है।<br>उपर्युक्त कथनों में से कौन-सा/से सही है/हैं? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"1 only","hi":"केवल 1"},"2":{"en":"2 only","hi":"केवल 2"},"3":{"en":"Both 1 and 2","hi":"1 और 2 दोनों"},"4":{"en":"None of these","hi":"इनमें से कोई नहीं"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – 1 only</b><br>The Himalayan states are earthquake-prone because the <b>Indian plate moves north/north-east and collides with the Eurasian plate</b>, building up stress (statement 1 correct). The Himalayas have no active volcanoes – India's only active volcano is <b>Barren Island</b> in the Andamans (statement 2 wrong). Hence <b><u>1 only</u></b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The Indian plate moves northward at about <b>5 cm per year</b>.<br>• Himalayan states and the North-East fall in <b>Seismic Zone V</b> (very high risk).<br>• India is divided into <b>four seismic zones (II–V)</b> by the BIS.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – केवल 1</b><br>हिमालयी राज्य भूकंप-प्रवण हैं क्योंकि <b>भारतीय प्लेट उत्तर/उत्तर-पूर्व की ओर खिसककर यूरेशियाई प्लेट से टकराती है</b>, जिससे तनाव बनता है (कथन 1 सही)। हिमालय में कोई सक्रिय ज्वालामुखी नहीं है – भारत का एकमात्र सक्रिय ज्वालामुखी अंडमान का <b>बैरन द्वीप</b> है (कथन 2 गलत)। अतः <b><u>केवल 1</u></b>।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• भारतीय प्लेट लगभग <b>5 cm प्रति वर्ष</b> की दर से उत्तर की ओर खिसक रही है।<br>• हिमालयी राज्य और पूर्वोत्तर <b>भूकंपीय क्षेत्र V</b> (अत्यधिक जोखिम) में आते हैं।<br>• BIS द्वारा भारत को <b>चार भूकंपीय क्षेत्रों (II–V)</b> में बाँटा गया है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":38,"local_id":"50038","quid":"Q1000072418","section":"GK","topic":"Ancient History: Gupta Dynasty","question":{"en":"What was the primary duty of the city <b>mayor (Nagara-Rakshaka or Pustapala)</b> in the Gupta dynasty's administration? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"गुप्त वंश के प्रशासन में नगर <b>महापौर (नगर-रक्षक या पुस्तपाल)</b> का प्रमुख कर्तव्य क्या था? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Managing military security and palace guards.","hi":"सैन्य सुरक्षा और महल रक्षकों का प्रबंधन।"},"2":{"en":"Supervising temple rituals and offerings.","hi":"मंदिर अनुष्ठानों और चढ़ावों की देखरेख।"},"3":{"en":"Recording land dimensions and urban governance.","hi":"भूमि मापों का अभिलेखन और नगरीय शासन।"},"4":{"en":"Leading merchant caravans on foreign trade missions.","hi":"विदेशी व्यापार अभियानों पर व्यापारी कारवाँ का नेतृत्व।"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Recording land dimensions and urban governance.</b><br>In Gupta administration, the <b>Pustapala</b> was the record-keeper who maintained <b>land records</b>, while the city officer looked after <b>urban governance</b>. So the duty was <b><u>recording land dimensions and urban governance</u></b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Gupta provinces were called <b>bhuktis</b> (under Uparika), districts <b>vishayas</b> (under Vishayapati).<br>• City administration was assisted by a council including the <b>Nagarashreshthi</b> (chief banker) and <b>Sarthavaha</b> (chief merchant).<br>• Gupta period saw an increase in <b>land grants</b> to Brahmins (agraharas).","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – भूमि मापों का अभिलेखन और नगरीय शासन।</b><br>गुप्त प्रशासन में <b>पुस्तपाल</b> अभिलेखपाल था जो <b>भूमि अभिलेख</b> रखता था, जबकि नगर अधिकारी <b>नगरीय शासन</b> देखता था। अतः कर्तव्य <b><u>भूमि मापों का अभिलेखन और नगरीय शासन</u></b> था।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• गुप्त प्रांतों को <b>भुक्ति</b> (उपरिक के अधीन) और ज़िलों को <b>विषय</b> (विषयपति के अधीन) कहा जाता था।<br>• नगर प्रशासन में <b>नगरश्रेष्ठि</b> (मुख्य बैंकर) और <b>सार्थवाह</b> (मुख्य व्यापारी) वाली परिषद सहायता करती थी।<br>• गुप्त काल में ब्राह्मणों को <b>भूमि अनुदान</b> (अग्रहार) बढ़े।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":39,"local_id":"50039","quid":"Q1000072419","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Sports(Static & Current)","question":{"en":"At which Summer Olympics did the Indian men’s hockey team fail to win a medal for the first time since 1928? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"1928 के बाद पहली बार भारतीय पुरुष हॉकी टीम किस ग्रीष्मकालीन ओलंपिक में पदक जीतने में विफल रही? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Montreal 1976","hi":"मॉन्ट्रियल 1976"},"2":{"en":"Munich 1972","hi":"म्यूनिख 1972"},"3":{"en":"Moscow 1980","hi":"मॉस्को 1980"},"4":{"en":"Los Angeles 1984","hi":"लॉस एंजिल्स 1984"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Montreal 1976</b><br>From 1928 to 1972, India won a hockey medal at every Olympics. At <b><u>Montreal 1976</u></b>, the first Olympics played on <b>artificial turf</b>, India finished <b>seventh</b> and failed to win a medal for the first time.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• India has won <b>8 Olympic gold medals</b> in hockey; the last at <b>Moscow 1980</b>.<br>• India won bronze at <b>Tokyo 2020</b> and <b>Paris 2024</b>.<br>• <b>Major Dhyan Chand</b>'s birthday (29 August) is celebrated as <b>National Sports Day</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – मॉन्ट्रियल 1976</b><br>1928 से 1972 तक भारत ने हर ओलंपिक में हॉकी पदक जीता। <b>कृत्रिम टर्फ</b> पर खेले गए पहले ओलंपिक <b><u>मॉन्ट्रियल 1976</u></b> में भारत <b>सातवें</b> स्थान पर रहा और पहली बार पदक नहीं जीत सका।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• भारत ने हॉकी में <b>8 ओलंपिक स्वर्ण</b> जीते हैं; अंतिम <b>मॉस्को 1980</b> में।<br>• भारत ने <b>टोक्यो 2020</b> और <b>पेरिस 2024</b> में कांस्य जीता।<br>• <b>मेजर ध्यानचंद</b> का जन्मदिन (29 अगस्त) <b>राष्ट्रीय खेल दिवस</b> के रूप में मनाया जाता है।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":40,"local_id":"50040","quid":"Q1000072420","section":"GK","topic":"Static GK: Books and Authors","question":{"en":"Which of the following statements correctly describes the award recognition received by the book 'The Mistress of Spices' written by Chitra Divakaruni? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"चित्रा दिवाकरुणी द्वारा लिखित पुस्तक 'द मिस्ट्रेस ऑफ स्पाइसेस' को प्राप्त पुरस्कार मान्यता का सही वर्णन निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा कथन करता है? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Received Booker Prize for South Asian politics","hi":"दक्षिण एशियाई राजनीति के लिए बुकर पुरस्कार मिला"},"2":{"en":"Won Sahitya Akademi Award for Indian English literature","hi":"भारतीय अंग्रेज़ी साहित्य के लिए साहित्य अकादमी पुरस्कार जीता"},"3":{"en":"Honored with Pulitzer Prize for immigrant struggles","hi":"आप्रवासी संघर्षों के लिए पुलित्ज़र पुरस्कार से सम्मानित"},"4":{"en":"Shortlisted for Women’s Prize for Fiction for magical realism and diaspora.","hi":"जादुई यथार्थवाद और प्रवासी विषय के लिए महिला कथा पुरस्कार हेतु शॉर्टलिस्ट हुई।"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (4) – Shortlisted for Women’s Prize for Fiction for magical realism and diaspora.</b><br><b>Chitra Banerjee Divakaruni</b>'s novel <b>The Mistress of Spices</b> (1997), a story of magical realism about an Indian immigrant in California, was <b><u>shortlisted for the Orange Prize (now Women's Prize for Fiction)</u></b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The novel was adapted into a 2005 film starring <b>Aishwarya Rai</b>.<br>• Her other works: <b>The Palace of Illusions</b> (Mahabharata from Draupadi's view), <b>Arranged Marriage</b> (American Book Award, 1996).<br>• The <b>Women's Prize for Fiction</b> was started in <b>1996</b> as the Orange Prize.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (4) – जादुई यथार्थवाद और प्रवासी विषय के लिए महिला कथा पुरस्कार हेतु शॉर्टलिस्ट हुई।</b><br><b>चित्रा बनर्जी दिवाकरुणी</b> का उपन्यास <b>द मिस्ट्रेस ऑफ स्पाइसेस</b> (1997), कैलिफ़ोर्निया में एक भारतीय आप्रवासी पर जादुई यथार्थवाद की कहानी, <b><u>ऑरेंज पुरस्कार (अब महिला कथा पुरस्कार) के लिए शॉर्टलिस्ट</u></b> हुआ।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• इस उपन्यास पर 2005 में <b>ऐश्वर्या राय</b> अभिनीत फ़िल्म बनी।<br>• उनकी अन्य रचनाएँ: <b>द पैलेस ऑफ इल्यूज़न्स</b> (द्रौपदी की दृष्टि से महाभारत), <b>अरेंज्ड मैरिज</b> (अमेरिकन बुक अवार्ड, 1996)।<br>• <b>महिला कथा पुरस्कार</b> <b>1996</b> में ऑरेंज पुरस्कार के रूप में शुरू हुआ।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":41,"local_id":"50041","quid":"Q1000072421","section":"GK","topic":"Geography: Agriculture","question":{"en":"Which of the following crop-season combinations is <b>incorrectly</b> matched? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा फसल-मौसम युग्म <b>गलत</b> सुमेलित है? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Rice – Kharif","hi":"चावल – खरीफ"},"2":{"en":"Wheat – Rabi","hi":"गेहूँ – रबी"},"3":{"en":"Cotton – Zaid","hi":"कपास – ज़ायद"},"4":{"en":"Mustard – Rabi","hi":"सरसों – रबी"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Cotton – Zaid</b><br><b>Cotton</b> is a <b>Kharif</b> crop, sown with the onset of the monsoon and harvested in autumn. So <b><u>Cotton – Zaid</u></b> is incorrectly matched.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>Kharif</b> (June–Oct): rice, maize, cotton, jute, groundnut, soybean.<br>• <b>Rabi</b> (Oct–March): wheat, barley, gram, mustard, peas.<br>• <b>Zaid</b> (March–June): watermelon, muskmelon, cucumber, fodder crops.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – कपास – ज़ायद</b><br><b>कपास</b> एक <b>खरीफ</b> फसल है, जो मानसून की शुरुआत में बोई और शरद ऋतु में काटी जाती है। अतः <b><u>कपास – ज़ायद</u></b> गलत सुमेलित है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>खरीफ</b> (जून–अक्टूबर): चावल, मक्का, कपास, जूट, मूँगफली, सोयाबीन।<br>• <b>रबी</b> (अक्टूबर–मार्च): गेहूँ, जौ, चना, सरसों, मटर।<br>• <b>ज़ायद</b> (मार्च–जून): तरबूज़, खरबूज़ा, खीरा, चारा फसलें।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":42,"local_id":"50042","quid":"Q1000072422","section":"GK","topic":"Geography: Minerals","question":{"en":"Why are thermal power plants in India commonly established close to coal mining areas? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"भारत में ताप विद्युत संयंत्र प्रायः कोयला खनन क्षेत्रों के पास क्यों स्थापित किए जाते हैं? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"For safety considerations","hi":"सुरक्षा कारणों से"},"2":{"en":"To minimize water consumption","hi":"जल की खपत कम करने के लिए"},"3":{"en":"To reduce environmental pollution","hi":"पर्यावरण प्रदूषण कम करने के लिए"},"4":{"en":"To lower transport costs","hi":"परिवहन लागत कम करने के लिए"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (4) – To lower transport costs</b><br>Coal is a <b>bulky, weight-losing raw material</b>. Setting up thermal plants near coalfields (<b>pit-head plants</b>) helps <b><u>lower transport costs</u></b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>NTPC</b> (1975) is India's largest power utility; its largest plant is at <b>Vindhyachal (MP)</b>.<br>• Coal-based thermal power provides about <b>70%</b> of India's electricity generation.<br>• Major coalfields: <b>Jharia</b> (largest), Raniganj, Bokaro, Korba, Talcher, Singrauli.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (4) – परिवहन लागत कम करने के लिए</b><br>कोयला <b>भारी, भार-ह्रासी कच्चा माल</b> है। कोयला क्षेत्रों के पास ताप संयंत्र (<b>पिट-हेड संयंत्र</b>) लगाने से <b><u>परिवहन लागत कम</u></b> होती है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>NTPC</b> (1975) भारत की सबसे बड़ी विद्युत कंपनी है; इसका सबसे बड़ा संयंत्र <b>विंध्याचल (म.प्र.)</b> में है।<br>• कोयला-आधारित ताप विद्युत भारत के बिजली उत्पादन का लगभग <b>70%</b> देती है।<br>• प्रमुख कोयला क्षेत्र: <b>झरिया</b> (सबसे बड़ा), रानीगंज, बोकारो, कोरबा, तालचेर, सिंगरौली।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":43,"local_id":"50043","quid":"Q1000072423","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: Emergency & Constitutional Amendment","question":{"en":"Which amendment introduced Article 246A to the Constitution? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"किस संशोधन ने संविधान में अनुच्छेद 246A जोड़ा? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"100<sup>th</sup> Amendment","hi":"100वाँ संशोधन"},"2":{"en":"101<sup>st</sup> Amendment","hi":"101वाँ संशोधन"},"3":{"en":"97<sup>th</sup> Amendment","hi":"97वाँ संशोधन"},"4":{"en":"99<sup>th</sup> Amendment","hi":"99वाँ संशोधन"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – 101<sup>st</sup> Amendment</b><br><b>Article 246A</b>, giving both Parliament and State Legislatures power to make <b>GST</b> laws, was inserted by the <b><u>101<sup>st</sup> Constitutional Amendment Act, 2016</u></b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• The 101<sup>st</sup> Amendment also added <b>Article 269A</b> (IGST) and <b>Article 279A</b> (GST Council).<br>• <b>100<sup>th</sup> Amendment (2015)</b> – India–Bangladesh Land Boundary Agreement.<br>• <b>99<sup>th</sup> Amendment (2014)</b> – NJAC (struck down in 2015); <b>97<sup>th</sup></b> – co-operative societies.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – 101वाँ संशोधन</b><br>संसद और राज्य विधानमंडलों दोनों को <b>GST</b> कानून बनाने की शक्ति देने वाला <b>अनुच्छेद 246A</b> <b><u>101वें संविधान संशोधन अधिनियम, 2016</u></b> द्वारा जोड़ा गया।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• 101वें संशोधन ने <b>अनुच्छेद 269A</b> (IGST) और <b>अनुच्छेद 279A</b> (GST परिषद) भी जोड़े।<br>• <b>100वाँ संशोधन (2015)</b> – भारत–बांग्लादेश भूमि सीमा समझौता।<br>• <b>99वाँ संशोधन (2014)</b> – NJAC (2015 में निरस्त); <b>97वाँ</b> – सहकारी समितियाँ।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":44,"local_id":"50044","quid":"Q1000072424","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: Making of Constitution","question":{"en":"How many members constituted the Board of Control under Pitt’s India Act? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"पिट्स इंडिया एक्ट के तहत नियंत्रण बोर्ड में कितने सदस्य थे? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Four members","hi":"चार सदस्य"},"2":{"en":"Five members","hi":"पाँच सदस्य"},"3":{"en":"Six members","hi":"छह सदस्य"},"4":{"en":"Seven members","hi":"सात सदस्य"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – Six members</b><br>The <b>Board of Control</b> under <b>Pitt's India Act, 1784</b> had <b><u>six members</u></b> – the Chancellor of the Exchequer, a Secretary of State and four Privy Councillors.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• It created a <b>system of double government</b> – Board of Control (political) and Court of Directors (commercial).<br>• The Governor-General's Council was reduced to <b>three members</b>.<br>• The Board of Control was abolished by the <b>Government of India Act, 1858</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – छह सदस्य</b><br><b>पिट्स इंडिया एक्ट, 1784</b> के तहत <b>नियंत्रण बोर्ड</b> में <b><u>छह सदस्य</u></b> थे – राजकोष का चांसलर, एक राज्य सचिव और चार प्रिवी काउंसलर।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• इसने <b>द्वैध शासन प्रणाली</b> बनाई – नियंत्रण बोर्ड (राजनीतिक) और निदेशक मंडल (वाणिज्यिक)।<br>• गवर्नर-जनरल की परिषद घटाकर <b>तीन सदस्यों</b> की कर दी गई।<br>• नियंत्रण बोर्ड को <b>भारत सरकार अधिनियम, 1858</b> द्वारा समाप्त किया गया।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":45,"local_id":"50045","quid":"Q1000072425","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: Local Government","question":{"en":"Under which article of the Indian Constitution is it mandatory to constitute a District Planning Committee (DPC) in every State? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"भारतीय संविधान के किस अनुच्छेद के तहत प्रत्येक राज्य में ज़िला योजना समिति (DPC) का गठन अनिवार्य है? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Article 243ZA","hi":"अनुच्छेद 243ZA"},"2":{"en":"Article 243ZB","hi":"अनुच्छेद 243ZB"},"3":{"en":"Article 243ZC","hi":"अनुच्छेद 243ZC"},"4":{"en":"Article 243ZD","hi":"अनुच्छेद 243ZD"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (4) – Article 243ZD</b><br><b><u>Article 243ZD</u></b> (added by the 74<sup>th</sup> Amendment) requires every State to constitute a <b>District Planning Committee</b> to consolidate the plans of Panchayats and Municipalities in the district.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• At least <b>four-fifths</b> of DPC members are elected from among elected members of district Panchayat and municipalities.<br>• <b>Article 243ZA</b> – elections to Municipalities; <b>243ZB</b> – application to UTs; <b>243ZC</b> – Part not to apply to certain areas.<br>• <b>Article 243ZE</b> – Metropolitan Planning Committee.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (4) – अनुच्छेद 243ZD</b><br><b><u>अनुच्छेद 243ZD</u></b> (74वें संशोधन द्वारा जोड़ा गया) प्रत्येक राज्य में ज़िले की पंचायतों और नगरपालिकाओं की योजनाओं को समेकित करने के लिए <b>ज़िला योजना समिति</b> के गठन को आवश्यक बनाता है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• DPC के कम से कम <b>चार-पाँचवें</b> सदस्य ज़िला पंचायत और नगरपालिकाओं के निर्वाचित सदस्यों में से चुने जाते हैं।<br>• <b>अनुच्छेद 243ZA</b> – नगरपालिकाओं के चुनाव; <b>243ZB</b> – केंद्रशासित प्रदेशों पर लागू होना; <b>243ZC</b> – कुछ क्षेत्रों पर भाग का लागू न होना।<br>• <b>अनुच्छेद 243ZE</b> – महानगर योजना समिति।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":46,"local_id":"50046","quid":"Q1000072426","section":"GK","topic":"Economics: Budget and Taxation","question":{"en":"Under which article of the Indian Constitution are both Parliament and State Legislatures granted the simultaneous power to make laws with respect to Goods and Services Tax (GST)? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"भारतीय संविधान के किस अनुच्छेद के तहत संसद और राज्य विधानमंडल दोनों को वस्तु एवं सेवा कर (GST) के संबंध में एक साथ कानून बनाने की शक्ति दी गई है? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Article 243B","hi":"अनुच्छेद 243B"},"2":{"en":"Article 246A","hi":"अनुच्छेद 246A"},"3":{"en":"Article 248","hi":"अनुच्छेद 248"},"4":{"en":"Article 254","hi":"अनुच्छेद 254"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Article 246A</b><br><b><u>Article 246A</u></b> gives <b>Parliament and State Legislatures simultaneous (concurrent) power</b> to make laws on GST; only Parliament can legislate on inter-state supply (IGST).<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• GST is a <b>dual GST</b> – CGST (Centre) and SGST (State) on intra-state supply.<br>• <b>Article 248</b> – residuary powers of Parliament; <b>Article 254</b> – inconsistency between Union and State laws.<br>• <b>Article 243B</b> – constitution of Panchayats.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – अनुच्छेद 246A</b><br><b><u>अनुच्छेद 246A</u></b> GST पर कानून बनाने के लिए <b>संसद और राज्य विधानमंडलों को एक साथ (समवर्ती) शक्ति</b> देता है; अंतर-राज्यीय आपूर्ति (IGST) पर केवल संसद कानून बना सकती है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• GST <b>दोहरा GST</b> है – राज्य के भीतर आपूर्ति पर CGST (केंद्र) और SGST (राज्य)।<br>• <b>अनुच्छेद 248</b> – संसद की अवशिष्ट शक्तियाँ; <b>अनुच्छेद 254</b> – संघ और राज्य कानूनों के बीच असंगति।<br>• <b>अनुच्छेद 243B</b> – पंचायतों का गठन।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":47,"local_id":"50047","quid":"Q1000072427","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: Centre-State Relations","question":{"en":"Under the Constitution of India, in which list of the Seventh Schedule does “Public Order” fall? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"भारत के संविधान के तहत “लोक व्यवस्था” सातवीं अनुसूची की किस सूची में आती है? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Residuary powers","hi":"अवशिष्ट शक्तियाँ"},"2":{"en":"Concurrent List","hi":"समवर्ती सूची"},"3":{"en":"State List","hi":"राज्य सूची"},"4":{"en":"Union List","hi":"संघ सूची"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – State List</b><br><b>\"Public order\"</b> is <b>Entry 1</b> and <b>\"Police\"</b> is <b>Entry 2</b> of the <b><u>State List (List II)</u></b> of the Seventh Schedule.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Union List has <b>100</b> subjects (originally 97), State List <b>61</b> (originally 66), Concurrent List <b>52</b> (originally 47).<br>• The <b>42<sup>nd</sup> Amendment (1976)</b> moved education, forests, weights and measures etc. to the Concurrent List.<br>• Residuary powers lie with <b>Parliament</b> (Article 248).","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – राज्य सूची</b><br><b>\"लोक व्यवस्था\"</b> सातवीं अनुसूची की <b><u>राज्य सूची (सूची II)</u></b> की <b>प्रविष्टि 1</b> और <b>\"पुलिस\"</b> <b>प्रविष्टि 2</b> है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• संघ सूची में <b>100</b> विषय (मूलतः 97), राज्य सूची में <b>61</b> (मूलतः 66), समवर्ती सूची में <b>52</b> (मूलतः 47)।<br>• <b>42वें संशोधन (1976)</b> ने शिक्षा, वन, माप-तौल आदि को समवर्ती सूची में डाला।<br>• अवशिष्ट शक्तियाँ <b>संसद</b> के पास हैं (अनुच्छेद 248)।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":48,"local_id":"50048","quid":"Q1000072428","section":"GK","topic":"Polity: New Criminal Laws 2023","question":{"en":"A warrant is issued for execution by a private person (not a police officer). During its execution, nearby civilians voluntarily assist because the person executing the warrant is actively pursuing the accused. Which of the following statements is legally correct under the Bharatiya Nagarik Suraksha Sanhita, 2023 in India? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"किसी वारंट को एक निजी व्यक्ति (पुलिस अधिकारी नहीं) द्वारा निष्पादित करने के लिए जारी किया जाता है। इसके निष्पादन के दौरान आसपास के नागरिक स्वेच्छा से सहायता करते हैं क्योंकि वारंट निष्पादित करने वाला व्यक्ति अभियुक्त का सक्रिय रूप से पीछा कर रहा है। भारतीय नागरिक सुरक्षा संहिता, 2023 के तहत निम्नलिखित में से कौन-सा कथन विधिक रूप से सही है? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Civilians cannot assist because only police may execute warrants.","hi":"नागरिक सहायता नहीं कर सकते क्योंकि केवल पुलिस वारंट निष्पादित कर सकती है।"},"2":{"en":"Assistance is lawful if the person to whom the warrant is directed is near at hand and acting in execution.","hi":"सहायता विधिसम्मत है यदि वह व्यक्ति, जिसे वारंट निर्दिष्ट है, निकट उपस्थित हो और निष्पादन में लगा हो।"},"3":{"en":"Civilian assistance requires prior magistrate approval.","hi":"नागरिक सहायता के लिए मजिस्ट्रेट की पूर्व स्वीकृति आवश्यक है।"},"4":{"en":"Only executive magistrates may assist in non-police warrant execution.","hi":"केवल कार्यपालक मजिस्ट्रेट गैर-पुलिस वारंट निष्पादन में सहायता कर सकते हैं।"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (2) – Assistance is lawful if the person to whom the warrant is directed is near at hand and acting in execution.</b><br>Under <b>Section 34 of BNSS</b> (old CrPC Sec. 38), when a warrant is directed to a person other than a police officer, any other person may aid in its execution <b><u>if the person to whom the warrant is directed is near at hand and acting in its execution</u></b>.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• <b>Section 33 BNSS</b> (old CrPC 37) – every person is bound to assist a Magistrate or police officer in certain cases.<br>• A Magistrate may direct a warrant to <b>any person</b> under special circumstances (old CrPC Sec. 73).<br>• BNSS has <b>531 sections</b> and replaced the CrPC from <b>1 July 2024</b>.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (2) – सहायता विधिसम्मत है यदि वह व्यक्ति, जिसे वारंट निर्दिष्ट है, निकट उपस्थित हो और निष्पादन में लगा हो।</b><br><b>BNSS की धारा 34</b> (पुरानी CrPC धारा 38) के अनुसार जब वारंट पुलिस अधिकारी से भिन्न व्यक्ति को निर्दिष्ट हो, तो कोई अन्य व्यक्ति उसके निष्पादन में सहायता कर सकता है <b><u>यदि वह व्यक्ति, जिसे वारंट निर्दिष्ट है, निकट उपस्थित हो और निष्पादन में लगा हो</u></b>।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• <b>BNSS धारा 33</b> (पुरानी CrPC 37) – कुछ मामलों में प्रत्येक व्यक्ति मजिस्ट्रेट या पुलिस अधिकारी की सहायता के लिए बाध्य है।<br>• विशेष परिस्थितियों में मजिस्ट्रेट <b>किसी भी व्यक्ति</b> को वारंट निर्दिष्ट कर सकता है (पुरानी CrPC धारा 73)।<br>• BNSS में <b>531 धाराएँ</b> हैं और इसने <b>1 जुलाई 2024</b> से CrPC का स्थान लिया।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":49,"local_id":"50049","quid":"Q1000072429","section":"GK","topic":"Economics: 1991 Reforms And Industrial policy","question":{"en":"Under India's economic reforms since 1991, disinvestment was undertaken mainly to achieve which of the following objectives? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"1991 से भारत के आर्थिक सुधारों के तहत विनिवेश मुख्य रूप से निम्नलिखित में से किस उद्देश्य की प्राप्ति के लिए किया गया? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Improve financial discipline and facilitate modernisation","hi":"वित्तीय अनुशासन में सुधार और आधुनिकीकरण को सुगम बनाना"},"2":{"en":"Expand industrial licensing and increase public ownership","hi":"औद्योगिक लाइसेंसिंग का विस्तार और सार्वजनिक स्वामित्व में वृद्धि"},"3":{"en":"Promote import substitution and restrict private investment","hi":"आयात प्रतिस्थापन को बढ़ावा और निजी निवेश पर प्रतिबंध"},"4":{"en":"Increase budgetary support and reduce market competition","hi":"बजटीय सहायता में वृद्धि और बाज़ार प्रतिस्पर्धा में कमी"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (1) – Improve financial discipline and facilitate modernisation</b><br>As per NCERT, disinvestment of PSUs was done mainly to <b><u>improve financial discipline and facilitate modernisation</u></b>, with private capital and managerial skills improving their performance.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• Disinvestment is managed by <b>DIPAM</b> under the Ministry of Finance.<br>• Proceeds go to the <b>National Investment Fund (NIF)</b>, set up in 2005.<br>• <b>Air India</b> was strategically sold to the <b>Tata Group</b> in 2021–22.","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (1) – वित्तीय अनुशासन में सुधार और आधुनिकीकरण को सुगम बनाना</b><br>NCERT के अनुसार PSU का विनिवेश मुख्यतः <b><u>वित्तीय अनुशासन सुधारने और आधुनिकीकरण को सुगम बनाने</u></b> के लिए किया गया, जिसमें निजी पूँजी और प्रबंधकीय कौशल से उनके प्रदर्शन में सुधार अपेक्षित था।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• विनिवेश का प्रबंधन वित्त मंत्रालय के अधीन <b>DIPAM</b> करता है।<br>• प्राप्त राशि 2005 में बने <b>राष्ट्रीय निवेश कोष (NIF)</b> में जाती है।<br>• <b>एयर इंडिया</b> को 2021–22 में <b>टाटा समूह</b> को रणनीतिक रूप से बेचा गया।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":50,"local_id":"50050","quid":"Q1000072430","section":"GK","topic":"Physics: Motion","question":{"en":"If the amplitude of an object undergoing simple harmonic motion is doubled while all other system parameters remain unchanged, how does its total mechanical energy change? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"यदि सरल आवर्त गति कर रही किसी वस्तु का आयाम दोगुना कर दिया जाए जबकि तंत्र के अन्य सभी प्राचल अपरिवर्तित रहें, तो उसकी कुल यांत्रिक ऊर्जा कैसे बदलती है? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"It remains the same","hi":"यह समान रहती है"},"2":{"en":"It becomes twice its original value","hi":"यह अपने मूल मान की दोगुनी हो जाती है"},"3":{"en":"It becomes four times its original value","hi":"यह अपने मूल मान की चार गुनी हो जाती है"},"4":{"en":"It becomes eight times its original value","hi":"यह अपने मूल मान की आठ गुनी हो जाती है"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Correct Answer: Option (3) – It becomes four times its original value</b><br>Total energy in SHM: \\(E = \\frac{1}{2}kA^2\\), so \\(E \\propto A^2\\)<br>If A becomes 2A, \\(E' = \\frac{1}{2}k(2A)^2 = 4E\\)<br>The energy becomes <b><u>four times</u></b> its original value.<br><br><br><b><u>Important Points:</u></b><br>• In SHM, total energy remains <b>constant</b>; KE is maximum at the mean position and PE is maximum at the extreme positions.<br>• Time period of a spring–mass system: \\(T = 2\\pi\\sqrt{\\frac{m}{k}}\\) – independent of amplitude.<br>• Simple pendulum: \\(T = 2\\pi\\sqrt{\\frac{l}{g}}\\).","hi":"<b>सही उत्तर: विकल्प (3) – यह अपने मूल मान की चार गुनी हो जाती है</b><br>सरल आवर्त गति में कुल ऊर्जा: \\(E = \\frac{1}{2}kA^2\\), अतः \\(E \\propto A^2\\)<br>A के 2A होने पर \\(E' = \\frac{1}{2}k(2A)^2 = 4E\\)<br>ऊर्जा अपने मूल मान की <b><u>चार गुनी</u></b> हो जाती है।<br><br><br><b><u>महत्वपूर्ण बिंदु:</u></b><br>• सरल आवर्त गति में कुल ऊर्जा <b>नियत</b> रहती है; माध्य स्थिति पर गतिज ऊर्जा और चरम स्थितियों पर स्थितिज ऊर्जा अधिकतम होती है।<br>• स्प्रिंग–द्रव्यमान तंत्र का आवर्तकाल: \\(T = 2\\pi\\sqrt{\\frac{m}{k}}\\) – आयाम से स्वतंत्र।<br>• सरल लोलक: \\(T = 2\\pi\\sqrt{\\frac{l}{g}}\\)।"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false}]},"MATH":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":51,"local_id":"50051","quid":"Q1000072431","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (3D)","question":{"en":"What is the volume of a sphere whose diameter is 56 cm? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"उस गोले का आयतन क्या है जिसका व्यास 56 cm है? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"92849.33 cm³"},"2":{"en":"86989.33 cm³"},"3":{"en":"81989.33 cm³"},"4":{"en":"91989.33 cm³"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"192\" height=\"192\" viewBox=\"0 0 192 192\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M26 96A70 22 0 0 0 166 96\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M26 96A70 22 0 0 1 166 96M96 96L150 51\"/><circle cx=\"96\" cy=\"96\" r=\"70\"/><circle cx=\"96\" cy=\"96\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"106\" y=\"57\">r = 28 cm</text></g></svg><br>\\(r = 28\\) cm<br>\\(V = \\frac{4}{3}\\pi r^3 = \\frac{4}{3} \\times \\frac{22}{7} \\times 28^3\\)<br>\\(= \\frac{4 \\times 22 \\times 21952}{21} = 91989.33\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{91989.33\\ \\text{cm}^3}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 91989.33 cm³.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"192\" height=\"192\" viewBox=\"0 0 192 192\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M26 96A70 22 0 0 0 166 96\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M26 96A70 22 0 0 1 166 96M96 96L150 51\"/><circle cx=\"96\" cy=\"96\" r=\"70\"/><circle cx=\"96\" cy=\"96\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"106\" y=\"57\">r = 28 cm</text></g></svg><br>\\(r = 28\\) cm<br>\\(V = \\frac{4}{3}\\pi r^3 = \\frac{4}{3} \\times \\frac{22}{7} \\times 28^3\\)<br>\\(= \\frac{4 \\times 22 \\times 21952}{21} = 91989.33\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{91989.33\\ \\text{cm}^3}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 91989.33 cm³ है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":52,"local_id":"50052","quid":"Q1000072432","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (3D)","question":{"en":"The space diagonal of a cuboid with dimensions 3 cm, 4 cm, and 12 cm is: [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"3 cm, 4 cm और 12 cm विमाओं वाले एक घनाभ का विकर्ण है: [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"13 cm"},"2":{"en":"14 cm"},"3":{"en":"11 cm"},"4":{"en":"5 cm"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"269\" height=\"113\" viewBox=\"-17 0 269 113\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M26 87L197 87M26 87L26 44M197 87L226 69M197 87L197 44M26 44L197 44M26 44L55 26M226 69L226 26M197 44L226 26M55 26L226 26\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M26 87L55 69M55 69L226 69M55 69L55 26M26 87L226 26\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"112\" y=\"103\">12 cm</text><text x=\"222\" y=\"99\">4 cm</text><text x=\"2\" y=\"70\">3 cm</text><text x=\"124\" y=\"54\">d</text></g></svg><br>Space diagonal \\(= \\sqrt{l^2 + b^2 + h^2}\\)<br>\\(= \\sqrt{9 + 16 + 144} = \\sqrt{169}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{13\\ \\text{cm}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 13 cm.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"269\" height=\"113\" viewBox=\"-17 0 269 113\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M26 87L197 87M26 87L26 44M197 87L226 69M197 87L197 44M26 44L197 44M26 44L55 26M226 69L226 26M197 44L226 26M55 26L226 26\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M26 87L55 69M55 69L226 69M55 69L55 26M26 87L226 26\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"112\" y=\"103\">12 cm</text><text x=\"222\" y=\"99\">4 cm</text><text x=\"2\" y=\"70\">3 cm</text><text x=\"124\" y=\"54\">d</text></g></svg><br>विकर्ण \\(= \\sqrt{l^2 + b^2 + h^2}\\)<br>\\(= \\sqrt{9 + 16 + 144} = \\sqrt{169}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{13\\ \\text{cm}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 13 cm है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":53,"local_id":"50053","quid":"Q1000072433","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (2D)","question":{"en":"The perimeter of an isosceles right-angled triangle is 2 + √2 cm. What is its area? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"एक समद्विबाहु समकोण त्रिभुज का परिमाप 2 + √2 cm है। उसका क्षेत्रफल क्या है? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"1 cm²"},"2":{"en":"0.5 cm²"},"3":{"en":"2 cm²"},"4":{"en":"3 cm²"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"222\" height=\"222\" viewBox=\"0 0 222 222\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M26 26L26 196L196 196ZM35 196L35 187L26 187\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"20\" y=\"17\">A</text><text x=\"15\" y=\"210\">B</text><text x=\"210\" y=\"206\">C</text><text x=\"14\" y=\"115\">a</text><text x=\"111\" y=\"212\">a</text><text x=\"124\" y=\"102\">a√2</text></g></svg><br>Let the equal legs be \\(a\\), then hypotenuse \\(= a\\sqrt{2}\\)<br>\\(2a + a\\sqrt{2} = 2 + \\sqrt{2} \\Rightarrow a = 1\\)<br>Area \\(= \\frac{1}{2} \\times 1 \\times 1 = \\boxed{0.5\\ \\text{cm}^2}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 0.5 cm².</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"222\" height=\"222\" viewBox=\"0 0 222 222\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M26 26L26 196L196 196ZM35 196L35 187L26 187\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"20\" y=\"17\">A</text><text x=\"15\" y=\"210\">B</text><text x=\"210\" y=\"206\">C</text><text x=\"14\" y=\"115\">a</text><text x=\"111\" y=\"212\">a</text><text x=\"124\" y=\"102\">a√2</text></g></svg><br>मान लीजिए बराबर भुजाएँ \\(a\\) हैं, तब कर्ण \\(= a\\sqrt{2}\\)<br>\\(2a + a\\sqrt{2} = 2 + \\sqrt{2} \\Rightarrow a = 1\\)<br>क्षेत्रफल \\(= \\frac{1}{2} \\times 1 \\times 1 = \\boxed{0.5\\ \\text{cm}^2}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 0.5 cm² है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":54,"local_id":"50054","quid":"Q1000072434","section":"MATH","topic":"Algebra","question":{"en":"If x + y = 20 and xy = 10, then find the value of x³ + y³. [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"यदि x + y = 20 और xy = 10 है, तो x³ + y³ का मान ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"2100"},"2":{"en":"2500"},"3":{"en":"7100"},"4":{"en":"7400"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"\\(x^3 + y^3 = (x + y)^3 - 3xy(x + y)\\)<br>\\(= 8000 - 3(10)(20) = 8000 - 600\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{7400}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 7400.</b>","hi":"\\(x^3 + y^3 = (x + y)^3 - 3xy(x + y)\\)<br>\\(= 8000 - 3(10)(20) = 8000 - 600\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{7400}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 7400 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":55,"local_id":"50055","quid":"Q1000072435","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (3D)","question":{"en":"What is the curved surface area of a cone with a radius of 7 cm and a slant height of 20 cm? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"7 cm त्रिज्या और 20 cm तिर्यक ऊँचाई वाले शंकु का वक्र पृष्ठीय क्षेत्रफल क्या है? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"520 cm²"},"2":{"en":"304 cm²"},"3":{"en":"340 cm²"},"4":{"en":"440 cm²"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"165\" height=\"222\" viewBox=\"0 0 165 222\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M26 178A57 18 0 0 0 139 178M26 178L83 26L139 178\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M26 178A57 18 0 0 1 139 178M83 178L139 178\"/><circle cx=\"83\" cy=\"178\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"111\" y=\"192\" font-size=\"11\">7 cm</text><text x=\"29\" y=\"96\">20 cm</text></g></svg><br>\\(CSA = \\pi r l = \\frac{22}{7} \\times 7 \\times 20\\)<br>\\(= 22 \\times 20 = \\boxed{440\\ \\text{cm}^2}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 440 cm².</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"165\" height=\"222\" viewBox=\"0 0 165 222\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M26 178A57 18 0 0 0 139 178M26 178L83 26L139 178\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M26 178A57 18 0 0 1 139 178M83 178L139 178\"/><circle cx=\"83\" cy=\"178\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"111\" y=\"192\" font-size=\"11\">7 cm</text><text x=\"29\" y=\"96\">20 cm</text></g></svg><br>\\(CSA = \\pi r l = \\frac{22}{7} \\times 7 \\times 20\\)<br>\\(= 22 \\times 20 = \\boxed{440\\ \\text{cm}^2}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 440 cm² है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":56,"local_id":"50056","quid":"Q1000072436","section":"MATH","topic":"Time Speed and Distance","question":{"en":"A person travels a certain distance at a speed of 5 km/h and completes the journey in 6 hours. If the speed is increased to 10 km/h, how much time will be taken to cover the same distance? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"एक व्यक्ति 5 km/h की गति से कोई दूरी तय करता है और यात्रा 6 घंटे में पूरी करता है। यदि गति 10 km/h कर दी जाए, तो वही दूरी तय करने में कितना समय लगेगा? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"2 hours","hi":"2 घंटे"},"2":{"en":"5 hours","hi":"5 घंटे"},"3":{"en":"3 hours","hi":"3 घंटे"},"4":{"en":"6 hours","hi":"6 घंटे"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Distance \\(= 5 \\times 6 = 30\\) km<br>Time at 10 km/h \\(= \\frac{30}{10}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{3\\ \\text{hours}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 3 hours.</b>","hi":"दूरी \\(= 5 \\times 6 = 30\\) km<br>10 km/h पर समय \\(= \\frac{30}{10}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{3\\ \\text{घंटे}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 3 घंटे है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":57,"local_id":"50057","quid":"Q1000072437","section":"MATH","topic":"Simplification and Approximation","question":{"en":"Find the value of: \\(2 + \\frac{1}{1 + \\frac{1}{1 + \\frac{1}{3}}}\\). [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"मान ज्ञात कीजिए: \\(2 + \\frac{1}{1 + \\frac{1}{1 + \\frac{1}{3}}}\\). [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"\\(\\frac{6}{7}\\)"},"2":{"en":"\\(\\frac{13}{7}\\)"},"3":{"en":"\\(\\frac{1}{5}\\)"},"4":{"en":"\\(\\frac{18}{7}\\)"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Innermost: \\(1 + \\frac{1}{3} = \\frac{4}{3}\\)<br>\\(1 + \\frac{1}{4/3} = 1 + \\frac{3}{4} = \\frac{7}{4}\\)<br>\\(2 + \\frac{1}{7/4} = 2 + \\frac{4}{7} = \\boxed{\\frac{18}{7}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): \\(\\frac{18}{7}\\).</b>","hi":"सबसे अंदर: \\(1 + \\frac{1}{3} = \\frac{4}{3}\\)<br>\\(1 + \\frac{1}{4/3} = 1 + \\frac{3}{4} = \\frac{7}{4}\\)<br>\\(2 + \\frac{1}{7/4} = 2 + \\frac{4}{7} = \\boxed{\\frac{18}{7}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): \\(\\frac{18}{7}\\) है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":58,"local_id":"50058","quid":"Q1000072438","section":"MATH","topic":"Number System","question":{"en":"If \\(\\sqrt{7^n} = 343\\), then the value of n is: [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"यदि \\(\\sqrt{7^n} = 343\\) है, तो n का मान है: [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"3"},"2":{"en":"8"},"3":{"en":"6"},"4":{"en":"5"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"\\(7^{n/2} = 7^3\\)<br>\\(\\frac{n}{2} = 3\\)<br>\\(n = \\boxed{6}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 6.</b>","hi":"\\(7^{n/2} = 7^3\\)<br>\\(\\frac{n}{2} = 3\\)<br>\\(n = \\boxed{6}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 6 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":59,"local_id":"50059","quid":"Q1000072439","section":"MATH","topic":"Number System","question":{"en":"If the 6-digit number 5z3x4y is divisible by 7, 11, and 13, find the value of (x + y − z). [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"यदि 6 अंकों की संख्या 5z3x4y, 7, 11 और 13 से विभाज्य है, तो (x + y − z) का मान ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"3"},"2":{"en":"2"},"3":{"en":"1"},"4":{"en":"4"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"Divisibility by 7, 11 and 13 together means divisibility by \\(7 \\times 11 \\times 13 = 1001\\)<br>A 6-digit number is divisible by 1001 only when it is of the form abcabc: \\(5z3x4y = 543543\\)<br>So \\(z = 4\\), \\(x = 5\\), \\(y = 3\\)<br>\\(x + y - z = 5 + 3 - 4 = \\boxed{4}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 4.</b>","hi":"7, 11 और 13 से विभाज्यता का अर्थ है \\(7 \\times 11 \\times 13 = 1001\\) से विभाज्यता<br>6 अंकों की संख्या 1001 से तभी विभाज्य होती है जब वह abcabc रूप की हो: \\(5z3x4y = 543543\\)<br>अतः \\(z = 4\\), \\(x = 5\\), \\(y = 3\\)<br>\\(x + y - z = 5 + 3 - 4 = \\boxed{4}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): 4 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":60,"local_id":"50060","quid":"Q1000072440","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"In △XYZ, G is the centroid and ZM is a median. If the segment GZ is 6 cm, what is the total length of the median ZM? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"△XYZ में, G केंद्रक है और ZM एक माध्यिका है। यदि खंड GZ = 6 cm है, तो माध्यिका ZM की कुल लंबाई क्या है? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"9 cm"},"2":{"en":"5 cm"},"3":{"en":"2 cm"},"4":{"en":"10 cm"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"282\" height=\"213\" viewBox=\"0 0 282 213\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M87 26L26 187L256 187ZM87 26L141 187M84 182l0 10M198 182l0 10\"/><circle cx=\"123\" cy=\"133\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"83\" y=\"17\">Z</text><text x=\"12\" y=\"198\">X</text><text x=\"271\" y=\"196\">Y</text><text x=\"141\" y=\"198\">M</text><text x=\"129\" y=\"139\" text-anchor=\"start\">G</text><text x=\"99\" y=\"84\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"11\">6</text><text x=\"122\" y=\"111\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"11\">ZM = ?</text></g></svg><br>Centroid divides the median in the ratio 2 : 1 from the vertex, so \\(GZ = \\frac{2}{3}ZM\\)<br>\\(ZM = \\frac{3}{2} \\times 6\\)<br>\\(ZM = \\boxed{9\\ \\text{cm}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 9 cm.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"282\" height=\"213\" viewBox=\"0 0 282 213\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M87 26L26 187L256 187ZM87 26L141 187M84 182l0 10M198 182l0 10\"/><circle cx=\"123\" cy=\"133\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"83\" y=\"17\">Z</text><text x=\"12\" y=\"198\">X</text><text x=\"271\" y=\"196\">Y</text><text x=\"141\" y=\"198\">M</text><text x=\"129\" y=\"139\" text-anchor=\"start\">G</text><text x=\"99\" y=\"84\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"11\">6</text><text x=\"122\" y=\"111\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-size=\"11\">ZM = ?</text></g></svg><br>केंद्रक माध्यिका को शीर्ष से 2 : 1 के अनुपात में विभाजित करता है, अतः \\(GZ = \\frac{2}{3}ZM\\)<br>\\(ZM = \\frac{3}{2} \\times 6\\)<br>\\(ZM = \\boxed{9\\ \\text{cm}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 9 cm है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":61,"local_id":"50061","quid":"Q1000072441","section":"MATH","topic":"Number System","question":{"en":"How many prime numbers p exist such that 120 < p < 150? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"ऐसे कितने अभाज्य संख्याएँ p हैं जिनके लिए 120 < p < 150 है? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"4"},"2":{"en":"7"},"3":{"en":"5"},"4":{"en":"6"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"Primes between 120 and 150: 127, 131, 137, 139, 149<br>Count \\(= \\boxed{5}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 5.</b>","hi":"120 और 150 के बीच अभाज्य संख्याएँ: 127, 131, 137, 139, 149<br>संख्या \\(= \\boxed{5}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 5 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":62,"local_id":"50062","quid":"Q1000072442","section":"MATH","topic":"Time Speed and Distance","question":{"en":"Ram and Shyam start moving simultaneously from points A and B toward each other at 9:00 a.m. After they cross paths, Ram takes 80 minutes to reach point B and Shyam takes 45 minutes to reach point A. At what specific time did they meet? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"राम और श्याम 9:00 a.m. पर बिंदु A और B से एक-दूसरे की ओर एक साथ चलना शुरू करते हैं। एक-दूसरे को पार करने के बाद राम को बिंदु B तक पहुँचने में 80 मिनट और श्याम को बिंदु A तक पहुँचने में 45 मिनट लगते हैं। वे किस समय मिले? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"9 : 30 am"},"2":{"en":"10 : 00 am"},"3":{"en":"10 : 30 am"},"4":{"en":"11 : 00 am"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Time after crossing: \\(t = \\sqrt{t_1 t_2} = \\sqrt{80 \\times 45}\\)<br>\\(= \\sqrt{3600} = 60\\) minutes<br>Meeting time \\(= 9{:}00 + 60\\) min \\(= \\boxed{10:00\\ \\text{am}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 10 : 00 am.</b>","hi":"मिलने के बाद का समय: \\(t = \\sqrt{t_1 t_2} = \\sqrt{80 \\times 45}\\)<br>\\(= \\sqrt{3600} = 60\\) मिनट<br>मिलने का समय \\(= 9{:}00 + 60\\) मिनट \\(= \\boxed{10:00\\ \\text{am}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 10 : 00 am है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":63,"local_id":"50063","quid":"Q1000072443","section":"MATH","topic":"Time and Work","question":{"en":"A can complete a certain work alone in 10 days, while B can complete the same work in 5 days. They work together for 2 days, after which B leaves and C joins A. A and C then complete the remaining work in 3 days. Find the number of days C would take to complete 40% of the work if working alone. [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"A किसी कार्य को अकेले 10 दिनों में पूरा कर सकता है, जबकि B वही कार्य 5 दिनों में पूरा कर सकता है। वे 2 दिन साथ कार्य करते हैं, फिर B चला जाता है और C, A के साथ जुड़ जाता है। A और C शेष कार्य 3 दिनों में पूरा करते हैं। यदि C अकेले कार्य करे तो कार्य का 40% पूरा करने में उसे कितने दिन लगेंगे? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"8 days","hi":"8 दिन"},"2":{"en":"10 days","hi":"10 दिन"},"3":{"en":"12 days","hi":"12 दिन"},"4":{"en":"16 days","hi":"16 दिन"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"\\(A = \\frac{1}{10}\\), \\(B = \\frac{1}{5}\\); 2 days together \\(= 2\\left(\\frac{1}{10} + \\frac{1}{5}\\right) = \\frac{3}{5}\\)<br>Remaining \\(= \\frac{2}{5}\\), done by A and C in 3 days \\(\\Rightarrow A + C = \\frac{2}{15}\\)<br>\\(C = \\frac{2}{15} - \\frac{1}{10} = \\frac{1}{30}\\)<br>40% of the work \\(= \\frac{0.4}{1/30} = \\boxed{12\\ \\text{days}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 12 days.</b>","hi":"\\(A = \\frac{1}{10}\\), \\(B = \\frac{1}{5}\\); 2 दिन साथ \\(= 2\\left(\\frac{1}{10} + \\frac{1}{5}\\right) = \\frac{3}{5}\\)<br>शेष \\(= \\frac{2}{5}\\), जो A और C ने 3 दिनों में किया \\(\\Rightarrow A + C = \\frac{2}{15}\\)<br>\\(C = \\frac{2}{15} - \\frac{1}{10} = \\frac{1}{30}\\)<br>कार्य का 40% \\(= \\frac{0.4}{1/30} = \\boxed{12\\ \\text{दिन}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 12 दिन है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":64,"local_id":"50064","quid":"Q1000072444","section":"MATH","topic":"Trigonometry","question":{"en":"Find the value of θ (0° < θ < 90°) if \\(\\frac{\\cos\\theta}{1 - \\sin\\theta} + \\frac{\\cos\\theta}{1 + \\sin\\theta} = 4\\). [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"θ का मान ज्ञात कीजिए (0° < θ < 90°) यदि \\(\\frac{\\cos\\theta}{1 - \\sin\\theta} + \\frac{\\cos\\theta}{1 + \\sin\\theta} = 4\\) है। [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"30°"},"2":{"en":"45°"},"3":{"en":"60°"},"4":{"en":"75°"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"\\(\\cos\\theta\\left[\\frac{2}{1 - \\sin^2\\theta}\\right] = \\frac{2\\cos\\theta}{\\cos^2\\theta} = \\frac{2}{\\cos\\theta} = 4\\)<br>\\(\\cos\\theta = \\frac{1}{2}\\)<br>\\(\\theta = \\boxed{60°}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 60°.</b>","hi":"\\(\\cos\\theta\\left[\\frac{2}{1 - \\sin^2\\theta}\\right] = \\frac{2\\cos\\theta}{\\cos^2\\theta} = \\frac{2}{\\cos\\theta} = 4\\)<br>\\(\\cos\\theta = \\frac{1}{2}\\)<br>\\(\\theta = \\boxed{60°}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 60° है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":65,"local_id":"50065","quid":"Q1000072445","section":"MATH","topic":"Height and Distance","question":{"en":"A vertical tower stands on a horizontal plane and is surmounted by a vertical flagstaff of height 6 m. At a point on the plane, the angle of elevation of the bottom of the flagstaff is 45° and that of the top of the flagstaff is 60°. Find the height of the tower. [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"एक ऊर्ध्वाधर मीनार क्षैतिज तल पर खड़ी है और उसके ऊपर 6 m ऊँचाई का ऊर्ध्वाधर ध्वजदंड है। तल पर एक बिंदु से ध्वजदंड के तल का उन्नयन कोण 45° और ध्वजदंड के शिखर का उन्नयन कोण 60° है। मीनार की ऊँचाई ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"\\(4(\\sqrt{3} + 1)\\) m"},"2":{"en":"\\(2(\\sqrt{3} + 1)\\) m"},"3":{"en":"\\(\\left(\\frac{3}{\\sqrt{3}} + 1\\right)\\) m"},"4":{"en":"\\(3(\\sqrt{3} + 1)\\) m"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"149\" height=\"202\" viewBox=\"-11 0 149 202\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M26 176L113 176M26 176L26 89M26 89L26 26M34 176L34 168L26 168M113 176L26 89M95 176A18 18 0 0 1 100 163M113 176L26 26M73 176A40 40 0 0 1 93 141\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"26\" y=\"16\">C</text><text x=\"14\" y=\"93\">A</text><text x=\"18\" y=\"187\">B</text><text x=\"14\" y=\"137\">h</text><text x=\"85\" y=\"169\" font-size=\"11\">45°</text><text x=\"78\" y=\"141\" font-size=\"11\">60°</text><text x=\"113\" y=\"190\">P</text><text x=\"69\" y=\"192\">d</text><text x=\"5\" y=\"62\">6 m</text></g></svg><br>Let the tower be \\(h\\) and the distance be \\(d\\): \\(\\tan 45° = \\frac{h}{d} \\Rightarrow d = h\\)<br>\\(\\tan 60° = \\frac{h + 6}{d} \\Rightarrow \\sqrt{3}h = h + 6\\)<br>\\(h(\\sqrt{3} - 1) = 6 \\Rightarrow h = \\frac{6}{\\sqrt{3} - 1} = \\frac{6(\\sqrt{3} + 1)}{2}\\)<br>\\(h = \\boxed{3(\\sqrt{3} + 1)\\ \\text{m}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): \\(3(\\sqrt{3} + 1)\\) m.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"149\" height=\"202\" viewBox=\"-11 0 149 202\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M26 176L113 176M26 176L26 89M26 89L26 26M34 176L34 168L26 168M113 176L26 89M95 176A18 18 0 0 1 100 163M113 176L26 26M73 176A40 40 0 0 1 93 141\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"26\" y=\"16\">C</text><text x=\"14\" y=\"93\">A</text><text x=\"18\" y=\"187\">B</text><text x=\"14\" y=\"137\">h</text><text x=\"85\" y=\"169\" font-size=\"11\">45°</text><text x=\"78\" y=\"141\" font-size=\"11\">60°</text><text x=\"113\" y=\"190\">P</text><text x=\"69\" y=\"192\">d</text><text x=\"5\" y=\"62\">6 m</text></g></svg><br>मान लीजिए मीनार \\(h\\) और दूरी \\(d\\) है: \\(\\tan 45° = \\frac{h}{d} \\Rightarrow d = h\\)<br>\\(\\tan 60° = \\frac{h + 6}{d} \\Rightarrow \\sqrt{3}h = h + 6\\)<br>\\(h(\\sqrt{3} - 1) = 6 \\Rightarrow h = \\frac{6}{\\sqrt{3} - 1} = \\frac{6(\\sqrt{3} + 1)}{2}\\)<br>\\(h = \\boxed{3(\\sqrt{3} + 1)\\ \\text{m}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (4): \\(3(\\sqrt{3} + 1)\\) m है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":66,"local_id":"50066","quid":"Q1000072446","section":"MATH","topic":"Trigonometry","question":{"en":"If tan θ = √5, find the value of \\(\\frac{\\operatorname{cosec}^2\\theta + \\sec^2\\theta}{\\operatorname{cosec}^2\\theta - \\sec^2\\theta}\\). [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"यदि tan θ = √5 है, तो \\(\\frac{\\operatorname{cosec}^2\\theta + \\sec^2\\theta}{\\operatorname{cosec}^2\\theta - \\sec^2\\theta}\\) का मान ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"\\(\\frac{3}{2}\\)"},"2":{"en":"\\(-\\frac{4}{5}\\)"},"3":{"en":"\\(-\\frac{3}{2}\\)"},"4":{"en":"\\(\\frac{4}{5}\\)"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"\\(\\operatorname{cosec}^2\\theta = 1 + \\cot^2\\theta = 1 + \\frac{1}{5} = \\frac{6}{5}\\), \\(\\sec^2\\theta = 1 + \\tan^2\\theta = 6\\)<br>\\(= \\frac{\\frac{6}{5} + 6}{\\frac{6}{5} - 6} = \\frac{36/5}{-24/5}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{-\\frac{3}{2}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): \\(-\\frac{3}{2}\\).</b>","hi":"\\(\\operatorname{cosec}^2\\theta = 1 + \\cot^2\\theta = 1 + \\frac{1}{5} = \\frac{6}{5}\\), \\(\\sec^2\\theta = 1 + \\tan^2\\theta = 6\\)<br>\\(= \\frac{\\frac{6}{5} + 6}{\\frac{6}{5} - 6} = \\frac{36/5}{-24/5}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{-\\frac{3}{2}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): \\(-\\frac{3}{2}\\) है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":67,"local_id":"50067","quid":"Q1000072447","section":"MATH","topic":"Algebra","question":{"en":"Given \\(x = \\frac{1}{2 - \\sqrt{3}}\\), find the value of \\(x - \\frac{1}{x}\\). [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"दिया गया है \\(x = \\frac{1}{2 - \\sqrt{3}}\\), तो \\(x - \\frac{1}{x}\\) का मान ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"\\(2\\sqrt{3}\\)"},"2":{"en":"\\(\\sqrt{3}\\)"},"3":{"en":"\\(5\\sqrt{3}\\)"},"4":{"en":"\\(\\sqrt{2}\\)"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"\\(x = \\frac{2 + \\sqrt{3}}{(2)^2 - 3} = 2 + \\sqrt{3}\\), so \\(\\frac{1}{x} = 2 - \\sqrt{3}\\)<br>\\(x - \\frac{1}{x} = (2 + \\sqrt{3}) - (2 - \\sqrt{3})\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{2\\sqrt{3}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): \\(2\\sqrt{3}\\).</b>","hi":"\\(x = \\frac{2 + \\sqrt{3}}{(2)^2 - 3} = 2 + \\sqrt{3}\\), अतः \\(\\frac{1}{x} = 2 - \\sqrt{3}\\)<br>\\(x - \\frac{1}{x} = (2 + \\sqrt{3}) - (2 - \\sqrt{3})\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{2\\sqrt{3}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): \\(2\\sqrt{3}\\) है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":68,"local_id":"50068","quid":"Q1000072448","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"Two equal parallel chords of a circle lie on opposite sides of the centre. The perpendicular distance between the chords is 6 cm. If the radius of the circle is 5 cm, find the length of each chord (in cm). [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"एक वृत्त की दो बराबर समांतर जीवाएँ केंद्र के विपरीत दिशाओं में स्थित हैं। जीवाओं के बीच लंबवत दूरी 6 cm है। यदि वृत्त की त्रिज्या 5 cm है, तो प्रत्येक जीवा की लंबाई (cm में) ज्ञात कीजिए। [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"8 cm"},"2":{"en":"10 cm"},"3":{"en":"12 cm"},"4":{"en":"16 cm"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"232\" height=\"232\" viewBox=\"0 0 232 232\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M44 62L188 62M44 170L188 170M122 62L122 68L116 68M122 170L122 164L116 164M116 116L188 62\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M116 62L116 170\"/><circle cx=\"116\" cy=\"116\" r=\"90\"/><circle cx=\"116\" cy=\"116\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"106\" y=\"118\">O</text><text x=\"156\" y=\"99\">5</text><text x=\"32\" y=\"58\">A</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"58\">B</text><text x=\"32\" y=\"182\">C</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"182\">D</text><text x=\"111\" y=\"93\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"11\">3</text><text x=\"111\" y=\"147\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"11\">3</text></g></svg><br>By symmetry each chord is 3 cm from the centre<br>Half chord \\(= \\sqrt{5^2 - 3^2} = 4\\) cm<br>Chord \\(= 2 \\times 4 = \\boxed{8\\ \\text{cm}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 8 cm.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"232\" height=\"232\" viewBox=\"0 0 232 232\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M44 62L188 62M44 170L188 170M122 62L122 68L116 68M122 170L122 164L116 164M116 116L188 62\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M116 62L116 170\"/><circle cx=\"116\" cy=\"116\" r=\"90\"/><circle cx=\"116\" cy=\"116\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"106\" y=\"118\">O</text><text x=\"156\" y=\"99\">5</text><text x=\"32\" y=\"58\">A</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"58\">B</text><text x=\"32\" y=\"182\">C</text><text x=\"200\" y=\"182\">D</text><text x=\"111\" y=\"93\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"11\">3</text><text x=\"111\" y=\"147\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-size=\"11\">3</text></g></svg><br>सममिति से प्रत्येक जीवा केंद्र से 3 cm दूर है<br>आधी जीवा \\(= \\sqrt{5^2 - 3^2} = 4\\) cm<br>जीवा \\(= 2 \\times 4 = \\boxed{8\\ \\text{cm}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 8 cm है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":69,"local_id":"50069","quid":"Q1000072449","section":"MATH","topic":"Mensuration (3D)","question":{"en":"The volume of a hemispherical bowl is 718⅔ cm³. A sphere is dropped into it such that the sphere's diameter is equal to the bowl's diameter. How much volume of the sphere remains outside the bowl? (Use π = 22/7) [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"एक अर्धगोलाकार कटोरे का आयतन 718⅔ cm³ है। इसमें एक गोला डाला जाता है जिसका व्यास कटोरे के व्यास के बराबर है। गोले का कितना आयतन कटोरे से बाहर रहता है? (π = 22/7 लीजिए) [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"811⅔ cm³"},"2":{"en":"820⅓ cm³"},"3":{"en":"718⅔ cm³"},"4":{"en":"732⅓ cm³"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"212\" height=\"212\" viewBox=\"0 0 212 212\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M26 106A80 80 0 0 0 186 106\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M186 106A80 80 0 0 0 26 106M106 106L186 106\"/><ellipse cx=\"106\" cy=\"106\" rx=\"80\" ry=\"26\"/><circle cx=\"106\" cy=\"106\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"146\" y=\"102\" font-size=\"11\">r</text><text x=\"106\" y=\"66\" font-size=\"11\">outside</text><text x=\"106\" y=\"154\" font-size=\"11\">bowl</text></g></svg><br>Sphere and bowl have the same diameter, so the sphere's volume \\(= 2 \\times\\) bowl volume<br>Outside volume \\(= 2 \\times 718\\frac{2}{3} - 718\\frac{2}{3} = 718\\frac{2}{3}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{718\\frac{2}{3}\\ \\text{cm}^3}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): 718⅔ cm³.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"212\" height=\"212\" viewBox=\"0 0 212 212\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M26 106A80 80 0 0 0 186 106\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M186 106A80 80 0 0 0 26 106M106 106L186 106\"/><ellipse cx=\"106\" cy=\"106\" rx=\"80\" ry=\"26\"/><circle cx=\"106\" cy=\"106\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"146\" y=\"102\" font-size=\"11\">r</text><text x=\"106\" y=\"66\" font-size=\"11\">outside</text><text x=\"106\" y=\"154\" font-size=\"11\">bowl</text></g></svg><br>गोले और कटोरे का व्यास समान है, अतः गोले का आयतन \\(= 2 \\times\\) कटोरे का आयतन<br>बाहर का आयतन \\(= 2 \\times 718\\frac{2}{3} - 718\\frac{2}{3} = 718\\frac{2}{3}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{718\\frac{2}{3}\\ \\text{cm}^3}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (3): 718⅔ cm³ है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":70,"local_id":"50070","quid":"Q1000072450","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"If the angle between two tangents drawn from a point P to a circle of radius 3 cm is 60°, what is the length of each tangent? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"एक बिंदु P से 3 cm त्रिज्या वाले वृत्त पर खींची गई दो स्पर्श रेखाओं के बीच का कोण 60° है, तो प्रत्येक स्पर्श रेखा की लंबाई क्या है? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"\\(3\\sqrt{3}\\) cm"},"2":{"en":"5 cm"},"3":{"en":"\\(4\\sqrt{2}\\) cm"},"4":{"en":"7 cm"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<svg width=\"277\" height=\"202\" viewBox=\"0 0 277 202\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M251 101L138 36M101 101L138 36M251 101L138 166M135 42L141 46L145 40M232 90A22 22 0 0 0 232 112\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M101 101L138 166M101 101L251 101\"/><circle cx=\"101\" cy=\"101\" r=\"75\"/><circle cx=\"101\" cy=\"101\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"91\" y=\"105\">O</text><text x=\"261\" y=\"105\">P</text><text x=\"146\" y=\"28\">A</text><text x=\"146\" y=\"182\">B</text><text x=\"112\" y=\"68\">3</text><text x=\"201\" y=\"61\">x</text><text x=\"219\" y=\"105\" font-size=\"11\">60°</text></g></svg><br>\\(OP\\) bisects the angle, so each half angle is 30°<br>\\(\\tan 30° = \\frac{3}{PT} \\Rightarrow PT = \\frac{3}{1/\\sqrt{3}}\\)<br>\\(PT = \\boxed{3\\sqrt{3}\\ \\text{cm}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): \\(3\\sqrt{3}\\) cm.</b>","hi":"<svg width=\"277\" height=\"202\" viewBox=\"0 0 277 202\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#000\" stroke-width=\"1.5\" font-size=\"12\"><path d=\"M251 101L138 36M101 101L138 36M251 101L138 166M135 42L141 46L145 40M232 90A22 22 0 0 0 232 112\"/><path stroke-dasharray=\"4 3\" d=\"M101 101L138 166M101 101L251 101\"/><circle cx=\"101\" cy=\"101\" r=\"75\"/><circle cx=\"101\" cy=\"101\" r=\"2\" fill=\"#000\"/><g fill=\"#000\" stroke=\"#fff\" stroke-width=\"3\" paint-order=\"stroke\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" text-anchor=\"middle\"><text x=\"91\" y=\"105\">O</text><text x=\"261\" y=\"105\">P</text><text x=\"146\" y=\"28\">A</text><text x=\"146\" y=\"182\">B</text><text x=\"112\" y=\"68\">3</text><text x=\"201\" y=\"61\">x</text><text x=\"219\" y=\"105\" font-size=\"11\">60°</text></g></svg><br>\\(OP\\) कोण को समद्विभाजित करता है, अतः प्रत्येक आधा कोण 30° है<br>\\(\\tan 30° = \\frac{3}{PT} \\Rightarrow PT = \\frac{3}{1/\\sqrt{3}}\\)<br>\\(PT = \\boxed{3\\sqrt{3}\\ \\text{cm}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): \\(3\\sqrt{3}\\) cm है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":71,"local_id":"50071","quid":"Q1000072451","section":"MATH","topic":"Trigonometry","question":{"en":"The hour hand of a clock moves from 3:00 to 7:00. What angle does it sweep in radians? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"घड़ी की घंटे वाली सुई 3:00 से 7:00 तक घूमती है। यह कितने रेडियन कोण घूमती है? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"\\(\\frac{2\\pi}{3}\\) radians","hi":"\\(\\frac{2\\pi}{3}\\) रेडियन"},"2":{"en":"\\(\\frac{\\pi}{3}\\) radians","hi":"\\(\\frac{\\pi}{3}\\) रेडियन"},"3":{"en":"\\(\\frac{2\\pi}{7}\\) radians","hi":"\\(\\frac{2\\pi}{7}\\) रेडियन"},"4":{"en":"\\(\\frac{\\pi}{7}\\) radians","hi":"\\(\\frac{\\pi}{7}\\) रेडियन"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"4 hours out of 12 \\(= \\frac{4}{12}\\) of a full turn<br>\\(= \\frac{1}{3} \\times 2\\pi = \\boxed{\\frac{2\\pi}{3}\\ \\text{radians}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): \\(\\frac{2\\pi}{3}\\) radians.</b>","hi":"12 में से 4 घंटे \\(= \\frac{4}{12}\\) पूर्ण चक्कर का<br>\\(= \\frac{1}{3} \\times 2\\pi = \\boxed{\\frac{2\\pi}{3}\\ \\text{रेडियन}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): \\(\\frac{2\\pi}{3}\\) रेडियन है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":72,"local_id":"50072","quid":"Q1000072452","section":"MATH","topic":"Time and Work","question":{"en":"Three friends, namely Krish, John and Leena, can do a particular work with equal efficiency. Krish works 'x' hours a day for 'x' days and then stops working. Then, John works 'y' hours a day for 'y' days. Then, Leena works 16 hours a day for 16 days and finally the work gets completed. Now, Leena alone can complete the work in 29 days by working 16 hours each day. If Krish, John and Leena together start doing the work with their respective per day working hours as mentioned, in how many days will the work be done (approximately)?<br>[Consider both 'x' and 'y' are integers] [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"तीन मित्र, कृष, जॉन और लीना, एक समान कार्यक्षमता से कोई कार्य कर सकते हैं। कृष 'x' घंटे प्रतिदिन 'x' दिनों तक कार्य करता है और फिर रुक जाता है। फिर जॉन 'y' घंटे प्रतिदिन 'y' दिनों तक कार्य करता है। फिर लीना 16 घंटे प्रतिदिन 16 दिनों तक कार्य करती है और अंत में कार्य पूरा हो जाता है। अब, लीना अकेले 16 घंटे प्रतिदिन कार्य करके 29 दिनों में कार्य पूरा कर सकती है। यदि कृष, जॉन और लीना उल्लिखित प्रति दिन कार्य घंटों के साथ मिलकर कार्य शुरू करें, तो कार्य कितने दिनों में पूरा होगा (लगभग)?<br>[मान लीजिए 'x' और 'y' दोनों पूर्णांक हैं] [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"11"},"2":{"en":"13"},"3":{"en":"15"},"4":{"en":"16"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Total work \\(= 29 \\times 16 = 464\\) hour-units<br>\\(x^2 + y^2 + 256 = 464 \\Rightarrow x^2 + y^2 = 208\\)<br>Integer solutions: \\(x = 8\\), \\(y = 12\\) (64 + 144 = 208)<br>Together, per day they work \\(8 + 12 + 16 = 36\\) hours, so days needed \\(= \\frac{464}{36} = 12.9 \\approx \\boxed{13}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 13.</b>","hi":"कुल कार्य \\(= 29 \\times 16 = 464\\) घंटा-इकाई<br>\\(x^2 + y^2 + 256 = 464 \\Rightarrow x^2 + y^2 = 208\\)<br>पूर्णांक हल: \\(x = 8\\), \\(y = 12\\) (64 + 144 = 208)<br>मिलकर प्रति दिन \\(8 + 12 + 16 = 36\\) घंटे, अतः आवश्यक दिन \\(= \\frac{464}{36} = 12.9 \\approx \\boxed{13}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 13 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":73,"local_id":"50073","quid":"Q1000072453","section":"MATH","topic":"Algebra","question":{"en":"If a² + b² = 57 and ab = 16, what is the absolute value of a − b? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"यदि a² + b² = 57 और ab = 16 है, तो |a − b| का मान क्या है? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"5"},"2":{"en":"57"},"3":{"en":"9"},"4":{"en":"73"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"\\((a - b)^2 = a^2 + b^2 - 2ab = 57 - 32 = 25\\)<br>\\(|a - b| = \\sqrt{25}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{5}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): 5.</b>","hi":"\\((a - b)^2 = a^2 + b^2 - 2ab = 57 - 32 = 25\\)<br>\\(|a - b| = \\sqrt{25}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{5}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (1): 5 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":74,"local_id":"50074","quid":"Q1000072454","section":"MATH","topic":"Number System","question":{"en":"Express the recurring decimal 0.416̄ (i.e., 0.41666...) as a fraction in its lowest terms. [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"आवर्ती दशमलव 0.416̄ (अर्थात् 0.41666...) को न्यूनतम पदों में भिन्न के रूप में व्यक्त कीजिए। [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"\\(\\frac{41}{99}\\)"},"2":{"en":"\\(\\frac{5}{12}\\)"},"3":{"en":"\\(\\frac{41}{90}\\)"},"4":{"en":"\\(\\frac{41}{100}\\)"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"\\(0.41666... = \\frac{41}{100} + \\frac{1}{150}\\)<br>Equivalently, \\(\\frac{416 - 41}{900} = \\frac{375}{900} = \\frac{5}{12}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{\\frac{5}{12}}\\)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): \\(\\frac{5}{12}\\).</b>","hi":"\\(0.41666... = \\frac{41}{100} + \\frac{1}{150}\\)<br>या, \\(\\frac{416 - 41}{900} = \\frac{375}{900} = \\frac{5}{12}\\)<br>\\(= \\boxed{\\frac{5}{12}}\\)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): \\(\\frac{5}{12}\\) है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":75,"local_id":"50075","quid":"Q1000072455","section":"MATH","topic":"Geometry","question":{"en":"Two circles with radii 6 cm and 3 cm have their centers 15 cm apart. How many common tangents can be drawn to these circles? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]","hi":"6 cm और 3 cm त्रिज्या वाले दो वृत्तों के केंद्र 15 cm की दूरी पर हैं। इन वृत्तों पर कितनी उभयनिष्ठ स्पर्श रेखाएँ खींची जा सकती हैं? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"2"},"2":{"en":"4"},"3":{"en":"1"},"4":{"en":"5"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"Sum of radii \\(= 6 + 3 = 9 < 15\\) and difference \\(= 3 < 15\\), so the circles are far apart (externally disjoint)<br>Externally disjoint circles have exactly \\(\\boxed{4}\\) common tangents (2 direct + 2 transverse)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 4.</b>","hi":"त्रिज्याओं का योग \\(= 6 + 3 = 9 < 15\\) और अंतर \\(= 3 < 15\\), अतः वृत्त बाहर से अलग हैं<br>ऐसे वृत्तों पर ठीक \\(\\boxed{4}\\) उभयनिष्ठ स्पर्श रेखाएँ होती हैं (2 सीधी + 2 तिर्यक)<br><br><b>अतः सही उत्तर विकल्प (2): 4 है।</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false}]},"ENGLISH":{"seconds":900,"questions":[{"no":76,"local_id":"50076","quid":"Q1000072456","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Passage","question":{"en":"Read the passage and answer the questions:<br><br>In the landscape of modern education, the choice between Arts, Commerce, and Science is not merely academic; it profoundly influences professional trajectories. Each stream offers a spectrum of career opportunities, responding to the evolving demands of the global economy.<br><br>The Arts stream, traditionally associated with creativity and critical thinking, leads to professions in journalism, law, international relations, and public policy. Graduates often assume roles such as content strategists, political analysts, legal advisors, and communication specialists. With interdisciplinary skills, Arts students increasingly permeate sectors once reserved for technical expertise, such as business consulting and digital marketing.<br><br>Commerce, characterized by its focus on trade, finance, and business management, offers access to careers in banking, corporate law, investment analysis, and entrepreneurship. Posts like chartered accountants, financial advisors, auditors, and marketing managers are quintessential to this domain. In an age of globalization, commerce graduates are pivotal to driving economic innovation and regulatory compliance.<br><br>Meanwhile, the Science stream remains the cornerstone of technological advancement and empirical research. From engineering and medicine to data science and biotechnology, science graduates occupy posts like research scientists, software developers, environmental consultants, and healthcare practitioners. Moreover, interdisciplinary branches such as AI and environmental engineering illustrate how scientific expertise continually adapts to societal needs.<br><br>While each field traditionally attracted distinct student profiles, contemporary career landscapes increasingly value hybrid skill sets. Thus, a student’s ability to integrate analytical rigor with creative and managerial acumen often defines success, blurring the once rigid lines between Arts, Commerce, and Science.<br><br><br><b>Identify the correct transformation of this sentence into passive voice:</b><br><br>\"Commerce offers access to careers in banking, corporate law, investment analysis, and entrepreneurship.\" [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Careers are accessed in banking, corporate law, investment analysis, and entrepreneurship by Commerce."},"2":{"en":"Careers in banking, corporate law, investment analysis, and entrepreneurship are offered by Commerce."},"3":{"en":"Careers are banking, corporate law, investment analysis, and entrepreneurship are offered by Commerce."},"4":{"en":"Careers are offering commerce access in banking, corporate law, investment analysis, and entrepreneurship."}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<i>\"Commerce … offers access to careers in banking, corporate law, investment analysis, and entrepreneurship.\"</i><br><b>Rule: Simple present active (V1/V5) → is/are + V3; the object becomes the subject.</b><br>Taking 'careers in banking…' as the object of 'offers', the passive is: Careers in banking, corporate law, investment analysis, and entrepreneurship <b>are offered</b> by Commerce.<br>Option 1 – 'are accessed' changes the verb<br>Option 3 – two verbs 'are … are' make it ungrammatical<br>Option 4 – 'are offering' is active continuous, not passive<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Careers in banking, corporate law, investment analysis, and entrepreneurship are offered by Commerce.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":77,"local_id":"50077","quid":"Q1000072457","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Passage","question":{"en":"Read the passage and answer the questions:<br><br>In the landscape of modern education, the choice between Arts, Commerce, and Science is not merely academic; it profoundly influences professional trajectories. Each stream offers a spectrum of career opportunities, responding to the evolving demands of the global economy.<br><br>The Arts stream, traditionally associated with creativity and critical thinking, leads to professions in journalism, law, international relations, and public policy. Graduates often assume roles such as content strategists, political analysts, legal advisors, and communication specialists. With interdisciplinary skills, Arts students increasingly permeate sectors once reserved for technical expertise, such as business consulting and digital marketing.<br><br>Commerce, characterized by its focus on trade, finance, and business management, offers access to careers in banking, corporate law, investment analysis, and entrepreneurship. Posts like chartered accountants, financial advisors, auditors, and marketing managers are quintessential to this domain. In an age of globalization, commerce graduates are pivotal to driving economic innovation and regulatory compliance.<br><br>Meanwhile, the Science stream remains the cornerstone of technological advancement and empirical research. From engineering and medicine to data science and biotechnology, science graduates occupy posts like research scientists, software developers, environmental consultants, and healthcare practitioners. Moreover, interdisciplinary branches such as AI and environmental engineering illustrate how scientific expertise continually adapts to societal needs.<br><br>While each field traditionally attracted distinct student profiles, contemporary career landscapes increasingly value hybrid skill sets. Thus, a student’s ability to integrate analytical rigor with creative and managerial acumen often defines success, blurring the once rigid lines between Arts, Commerce, and Science.<br><br><br>Choose the option where the use of the relative pronoun is grammatically incorrect. [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Graduates who pursue interdisciplinary skills are highly valued."},"2":{"en":"Posts which involve financial planning require precision."},"3":{"en":"Students whom excel at both analysis and creativity are rare."},"4":{"en":"Professionals whose expertise spans multiple domains are in demand."}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: 'who' is the subject form; 'whom' is the object form.</b><br>In option 3 the relative pronoun is the subject of 'excel', so it must be 'who': Students <b>who</b> excel at both analysis and creativity are rare.<br>Option 1 – 'who' is the subject of 'pursue' – correct<br>Option 2 – 'which' for things – correct<br>Option 4 – 'whose' shows possession – correct<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Students whom excel at both analysis and creativity are rare.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":78,"local_id":"50078","quid":"Q1000072458","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Passage","question":{"en":"Read the passage and answer the questions:<br><br>In the landscape of modern education, the choice between Arts, Commerce, and Science is not merely academic; it profoundly influences professional trajectories. Each stream offers a spectrum of career opportunities, responding to the evolving demands of the global economy.<br><br>The Arts stream, traditionally associated with creativity and critical thinking, leads to professions in journalism, law, international relations, and public policy. Graduates often assume roles such as content strategists, political analysts, legal advisors, and communication specialists. With interdisciplinary skills, Arts students increasingly permeate sectors once reserved for technical expertise, such as business consulting and digital marketing.<br><br>Commerce, characterized by its focus on trade, finance, and business management, offers access to careers in banking, corporate law, investment analysis, and entrepreneurship. Posts like chartered accountants, financial advisors, auditors, and marketing managers are quintessential to this domain. In an age of globalization, commerce graduates are pivotal to driving economic innovation and regulatory compliance.<br><br>Meanwhile, the Science stream remains the cornerstone of technological advancement and empirical research. From engineering and medicine to data science and biotechnology, science graduates occupy posts like research scientists, software developers, environmental consultants, and healthcare practitioners. Moreover, interdisciplinary branches such as AI and environmental engineering illustrate how scientific expertise continually adapts to societal needs.<br><br>While each field traditionally attracted distinct student profiles, contemporary career landscapes increasingly value hybrid skill sets. Thus, a student’s ability to integrate analytical rigor with creative and managerial acumen often defines success, blurring the once rigid lines between Arts, Commerce, and Science.<br><br><br>Choose the word that is closest in meaning to \"permeate\" as used in the passage. [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Exclude"},"2":{"en":"Spread"},"3":{"en":"Conceal"},"4":{"en":"Defeat"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<i>\"With interdisciplinary skills, Arts students increasingly permeate sectors once reserved for technical expertise…\"</i><br><b>Permeate (फैल जाना, व्याप्त होना)</b> = to spread through. Arts students are spreading into new sectors.<br><b>Spread (फैलना)</b> ✔<br><b>Exclude (बाहर रखना)</b> – opposite<br><b>Conceal (छिपाना)</b> – unrelated<br><b>Defeat (हराना)</b> – unrelated<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Spread.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":79,"local_id":"50079","quid":"Q1000072459","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Passage","question":{"en":"Read the passage and answer the questions:<br><br>In the landscape of modern education, the choice between Arts, Commerce, and Science is not merely academic; it profoundly influences professional trajectories. Each stream offers a spectrum of career opportunities, responding to the evolving demands of the global economy.<br><br>The Arts stream, traditionally associated with creativity and critical thinking, leads to professions in journalism, law, international relations, and public policy. Graduates often assume roles such as content strategists, political analysts, legal advisors, and communication specialists. With interdisciplinary skills, Arts students increasingly permeate sectors once reserved for technical expertise, such as business consulting and digital marketing.<br><br>Commerce, characterized by its focus on trade, finance, and business management, offers access to careers in banking, corporate law, investment analysis, and entrepreneurship. Posts like chartered accountants, financial advisors, auditors, and marketing managers are quintessential to this domain. In an age of globalization, commerce graduates are pivotal to driving economic innovation and regulatory compliance.<br><br>Meanwhile, the Science stream remains the cornerstone of technological advancement and empirical research. From engineering and medicine to data science and biotechnology, science graduates occupy posts like research scientists, software developers, environmental consultants, and healthcare practitioners. Moreover, interdisciplinary branches such as AI and environmental engineering illustrate how scientific expertise continually adapts to societal needs.<br><br>While each field traditionally attracted distinct student profiles, contemporary career landscapes increasingly value hybrid skill sets. Thus, a student’s ability to integrate analytical rigor with creative and managerial acumen often defines success, blurring the once rigid lines between Arts, Commerce, and Science.<br><br><br>In the phrase \"interdisciplinary branches,\" what does \"interdisciplinary\" most nearly mean? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Related to one subject only"},"2":{"en":"Combining multiple areas of study"},"3":{"en":"Opposing different disciplines"},"4":{"en":"Excluding sciences and arts"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<i>\"…interdisciplinary branches such as AI and environmental engineering illustrate how scientific expertise continually adapts…\"</i><br><b>Interdisciplinary (अंतर्विषयक)</b> = involving two or more fields of study. AI and environmental engineering join several fields.<br>Related to one subject only – opposite<br>Opposing different disciplines – the prefix 'inter' means between, not against<br>Excluding sciences and arts – unrelated<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Combining multiple areas of study.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":80,"local_id":"50080","quid":"Q1000072460","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Passage","question":{"en":"Read the passage and answer the questions:<br><br>In the landscape of modern education, the choice between Arts, Commerce, and Science is not merely academic; it profoundly influences professional trajectories. Each stream offers a spectrum of career opportunities, responding to the evolving demands of the global economy.<br><br>The Arts stream, traditionally associated with creativity and critical thinking, leads to professions in journalism, law, international relations, and public policy. Graduates often assume roles such as content strategists, political analysts, legal advisors, and communication specialists. With interdisciplinary skills, Arts students increasingly permeate sectors once reserved for technical expertise, such as business consulting and digital marketing.<br><br>Commerce, characterized by its focus on trade, finance, and business management, offers access to careers in banking, corporate law, investment analysis, and entrepreneurship. Posts like chartered accountants, financial advisors, auditors, and marketing managers are quintessential to this domain. In an age of globalization, commerce graduates are pivotal to driving economic innovation and regulatory compliance.<br><br>Meanwhile, the Science stream remains the cornerstone of technological advancement and empirical research. From engineering and medicine to data science and biotechnology, science graduates occupy posts like research scientists, software developers, environmental consultants, and healthcare practitioners. Moreover, interdisciplinary branches such as AI and environmental engineering illustrate how scientific expertise continually adapts to societal needs.<br><br>While each field traditionally attracted distinct student profiles, contemporary career landscapes increasingly value hybrid skill sets. Thus, a student’s ability to integrate analytical rigor with creative and managerial acumen often defines success, blurring the once rigid lines between Arts, Commerce, and Science.<br><br><br>Which of the following best reflects the main idea of the passage? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Science students have better career options than Arts students."},"2":{"en":"Arts, Commerce, and Science fields are now overlapping, and hybrid skills are becoming important."},"3":{"en":"Commerce dominates the modern economy."},"4":{"en":"Career paths have remained rigidly tied to educational streams."}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<i>\"…contemporary career landscapes increasingly value hybrid skill sets… blurring the once rigid lines between Arts, Commerce, and Science.\"</i><br>The passage describes all three streams and concludes that they now overlap and hybrid skills matter.<br>Option 1 – no stream is ranked above another<br>Option 3 – Commerce is one of three; not shown as dominant<br>Option 4 – opposite of 'blurring the once rigid lines'<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): Arts, Commerce, and Science fields are now overlapping, and hybrid skills are becoming important.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":81,"local_id":"50081","quid":"Q1000072461","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Fill in the Blanks","question":{"en":"Complete the collocation by choosing a suitable word to fill in the blank.<br><br>The researchers meticulously ______ the parameters for the study. [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"delineated"},"2":{"en":"decorated"},"3":{"en":"deviated"},"4":{"en":"deliberated"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: 'delineate the parameters' is a standard collocation in research writing.</b><br><b>Delineated (स्पष्ट रूप से निर्धारित किया)</b> = described or marked out precisely – suits 'meticulously'.<br>Correct sentence: The researchers meticulously <b>delineated</b> the parameters for the study.<br><b>Decorated (सजाया)</b> – meaningless with parameters<br><b>Deviated (भटका)</b> – intransitive; needs 'from'<br><b>Deliberated (विचार-विमर्श किया)</b> – usually takes 'on/over', not a direct object<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): delineated.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":82,"local_id":"50082","quid":"Q1000072462","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Para Jumbles (PQRS)","question":{"en":"Rearrange the parts of the sentence in the correct order.<br><br>Following the approval of a groundbreaking cancer therapy,<br>P. while skeptics warned of the long-term side effects and limited accessibility for low-income patients,<br>Q. oncologists and researchers hailed the innovation as a paradigm shift in cancer treatment,<br>R. leading to global discussions on the affordability and regulatory challenges of the new treatment<br>S. as early trials demonstrated unprecedented success in eliminating aggressive tumors, [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"PQRS"},"2":{"en":"SQRP"},"3":{"en":"QSPR"},"4":{"en":"QPSR"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Order: QPSR</b><br><b>Q</b> gives the main clause: 'oncologists and researchers hailed the innovation…'.<br><b>P</b> 'while skeptics warned of the long-term side effects…' gives the contrasting view.<br><b>S</b> 'as early trials demonstrated unprecedented success…' gives the background.<br><b>R</b> 'leading to global discussions…' states the result and ends the sentence (no comma at the end).<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): QPSR.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":83,"local_id":"50083","quid":"Q1000072463","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Phrasal Verbs","question":{"en":"Fill in the blank with an appropriate phrasal verb.<br><br>If you’re serious about your goals, you must ______ all distractions. [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"cast off"},"2":{"en":"cast down"},"3":{"en":"caste away"},"4":{"en":"caste over"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Cast off (त्याग देना) = to get rid of something unwanted.</b><br>A person serious about goals must throw away distractions.<br>Correct sentence: …you must <b>cast off</b> all distractions.<br><b>Cast down (उदास करना; नीचे फेंकना)</b> = to make sad or to throw down<br><b>caste away / caste over</b> – 'caste' (जाति) is a noun meaning social class; these are not phrasal verbs<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): cast off.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":84,"local_id":"50084","quid":"Q1000072464","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Para Jumbles (PQRS)","question":{"en":"Rearrange the parts of the sentence in the correct order.<br><br>The ethical dilemmas in scientific research<br>P. have sparked ongoing debates among scholars,<br>Q. concerning genetic modifications and bioengineering,<br>R. as technological advancements outpace regulatory frameworks<br>S. raising concerns about moral boundaries and unintended consequences [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"QPRS"},"2":{"en":"SPRQ"},"3":{"en":"PRQS"},"4":{"en":"SQPR"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Order: PRQS</b><br><b>P</b> 'have sparked ongoing debates among scholars,' gives the verb for 'The ethical dilemmas…'.<br><b>R</b> 'as technological advancements outpace regulatory frameworks' gives the reason.<br><b>Q</b> 'concerning genetic modifications and bioengineering,' names the area.<br><b>S</b> 'raising concerns about moral boundaries…' ends with the result.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): PRQS.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":85,"local_id":"50085","quid":"Q1000072465","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Idioms and Phrases","question":{"en":"What does the idiom \"Red letter day\" mean? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"A day of great significance or celebration"},"2":{"en":"A day of financial loss"},"3":{"en":"A day of regret and sadness"},"4":{"en":"A day of strict discipline"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Red letter day (यादगार/शुभ दिन) = a day that is special or important, usually happy.</b><br>Example: The day she cleared the exam was a red letter day for her family.<br>A day of financial loss (आर्थिक हानि का दिन) – 'in the red' refers to loss, not this idiom<br>A day of regret (पछतावे का दिन) – opposite<br>A day of strict discipline (अनुशासन का दिन) – unrelated<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): A day of great significance or celebration.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":86,"local_id":"50086","quid":"Q1000072466","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spotting Errors","question":{"en":"Identify the error in the sentence.<br><br>He paid a heavy apology after the incident. [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"apology"},"2":{"en":"paid"},"3":{"en":"heavy"},"4":{"en":"incident"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: 'apology' collocates with adjectives like 'sincere', 'deep' or 'profuse', not 'heavy'.</b><br>'heavy' goes with words like 'price', 'loss' or 'fine' (a heavy price), so it is the wrong adjective here.<br>Correct sentence: He paid a <b>sincere</b> apology after the incident.<br>'paid' – 'pay one's apologies' is an accepted formal expression<br>'apology' and 'incident' are correct nouns<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): heavy.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":87,"local_id":"50087","quid":"Q1000072467","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Homophones and Homonyms","question":{"en":"Which of the following options is NOT one of the meanings of the homonym 'subject'? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"To freely exclude oneself from external governance or control"},"2":{"en":"A branch of knowledge studied or taught in school or university"},"3":{"en":"A person under the rule of a monarch or sovereign state"},"4":{"en":"To cause or force someone to undergo an unpleasant experience"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Subject (विषय; प्रजा; अधीन करना) – a homonym with several meanings.</b><br>A branch of knowledge: 'English is my favourite subject' – valid<br>A person under a ruler: 'British subjects' – valid<br>To make someone undergo something unpleasant: 'subjected to torture' – valid<br>Freely excluding oneself from control is the opposite of being a subject, so it is NOT a meaning.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): To freely exclude oneself from external governance or control.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":88,"local_id":"50088","quid":"Q1000072468","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Idioms and Phrases","question":{"en":"Choose the correct idiom for the word highlighted in bold.<br><br>\"Kavita told her manager that she planned to leave the company, but after the manager offered her a pay raise, she had <b>a change of heart</b> and agreed to stay.\" [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"To become physically unwell due to stress"},"2":{"en":"To change one’s feelings or decision about something"},"3":{"en":"To get emotional during a conversation"},"4":{"en":"To start working harder to get promoted"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>A change of heart (मन बदल जाना) = a change in one's opinion or decision.</b><br>Kavita first planned to leave, then decided to stay.<br>Example: After meeting the family, he had a change of heart about the marriage.<br>Physically unwell (शारीरिक रूप से अस्वस्थ) – literal reading of 'heart'<br>Get emotional (भावुक होना) – unrelated<br>Work harder (अधिक मेहनत करना) – unrelated<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): To change one’s feelings or decision about something.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":89,"local_id":"50089","quid":"Q1000072469","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Para Jumbles (PQRS)","question":{"en":"<b>Which of the given options arranges the following sentences in the most logical sequence to form a meaningful paragraph?</b><br><br>1. Philosophers debate the role of experience, reason and perception in the acquisition of knowledge.<br>2. The nature of knowledge is a central concern in philosophy, particularly in the field of epistemology.<br>3. Some argue that knowledge comes from sensory experiences, while others believe in the primacy of reason or innate ideas.<br>4. Epistemology explores the sources, limits and validity of knowledge, asking questions like “What can we know?”<br>5. Ultimately, understanding knowledge involves examining the relationship between the knower, the known and the process of knowing. [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"3-1-2-4-5"},"2":{"en":"2-4-1-3-5"},"3":{"en":"4-3-1-2-5"},"4":{"en":"5-2-1-3-4"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Order: 2-4-1-3-5</b><br><b>2</b> introduces the topic and the term 'epistemology'.<br><b>4</b> defines epistemology.<br><b>1</b> 'Philosophers debate the role of experience, reason…' introduces the debate.<br><b>3</b> 'Some argue … others believe…' explains both sides.<br><b>5</b> 'Ultimately' concludes.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): 2-4-1-3-5.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":90,"local_id":"50090","quid":"Q1000072470","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Para Jumbles (PQRS)","question":{"en":"<b>Which of the given options arranges the following sentences in the most logical sequence to form a meaningful paragraph?</b><br><br>1. Predators evolve sharper claws, faster speeds, or enhanced hunting techniques to catch prey more effectively.<br>2. This cycle of adaptation and counter-adaptation drives the continuous evolution of both groups.<br>3. In response, prey species develop defensive adaptations such as camouflage, speed, or toxic chemicals.<br>4. The concept of an evolutionary arms race describes the ongoing adaptations between predators and prey.<br>5. Such evolutionary arms races are seen in species like cheetahs and gazelles or venomous snakes and resistant prey. [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"3-4-2-1-5"},"2":{"en":"1-4-5-3-2"},"3":{"en":"2-1-3-5-4"},"4":{"en":"4-1-3-2-5"}},"answer":"4","solution":{"en":"<b>Order: 4-1-3-2-5</b><br><b>4</b> introduces the concept of an evolutionary arms race.<br><b>1</b> describes the predators' adaptations.<br><b>3</b> 'In response' gives the prey's adaptations.<br><b>2</b> 'This cycle…' sums up 1 and 3.<br><b>5</b> 'Such evolutionary arms races…' gives examples to close.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (4): 4-1-3-2-5.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":91,"local_id":"50091","quid":"Q1000072471","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Synonym","question":{"en":"Select the most appropriate synonym of the given word: <b>MENDACIOUS</b> [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Honest"},"2":{"en":"Truthful"},"3":{"en":"Dishonest"},"4":{"en":"Candid"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Mendacious (झूठा, असत्यवादी) = not telling the truth; lying.</b><br><b>Dishonest (बेईमान)</b> ✔<br><b>Honest (ईमानदार)</b> – antonym<br><b>Truthful (सच्चा)</b> – antonym<br><b>Candid (स्पष्टवादी)</b> = frank – antonym<br>More synonyms: deceitful, untruthful, lying.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Dishonest.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":92,"local_id":"50092","quid":"Q1000072472","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Synonym","question":{"en":"Select the most appropriate synonym of the given word: <b>IMBRUE</b> [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"To cleanse"},"2":{"en":"To soak"},"3":{"en":"To purify"},"4":{"en":"To expel"}},"answer":"2","solution":{"en":"<b>Imbrue (भिगोना, सराबोर करना) = to soak or stain, especially with blood.</b><br><b>To soak (भिगोना)</b> ✔<br><b>To cleanse (साफ़ करना)</b> – opposite of staining<br><b>To purify (शुद्ध करना)</b> – opposite sense<br><b>To expel (निकालना)</b> – unrelated<br>More synonyms: drench, saturate, steep.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (2): To soak.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":93,"local_id":"50093","quid":"Q1000072473","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Antonym","question":{"en":"Select the most appropriate antonym of the given word<b>. Altruism</b> [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Selflessness"},"2":{"en":"Generosity"},"3":{"en":"Egoism"},"4":{"en":"Charity"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Altruism (परोपकार) = selfless concern for the well-being of others.</b><br><b>Egoism (अहंवाद, स्वार्थ)</b> = concern only for oneself ✔<br><b>Selflessness (निःस्वार्थता)</b> – synonym<br><b>Generosity (उदारता)</b> – synonym<br><b>Charity (दान)</b> – synonym<br>More antonyms: selfishness, self-interest, egotism.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Egoism.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":94,"local_id":"50094","quid":"Q1000072474","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spelling Check","question":{"en":"Which is the <b>correct spelling</b> for a word meaning 'without equal or unmatched'? [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Incomparable"},"2":{"en":"Incomparible"},"3":{"en":"Incompareable"},"4":{"en":"Incomperable"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Incomparable (अतुलनीय) = without an equal; matchless.</b><br>Spelling: in-com-<b>par</b>-<b>able</b>.<br><b>Incomparible</b> – '-ible' in place of '-able'<br><b>Incompareable</b> – extra 'e' before '-able'<br><b>Incomperable</b> – 'e' in place of 'a' (-per-)<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Incomparable.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":95,"local_id":"50095","quid":"Q1000072475","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Spelling Check","question":{"en":"Identify the <b>misspelt</b> word. [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Apostrophize"},"2":{"en":"Ethereal"},"3":{"en":"Munificense"},"4":{"en":"Penumbra"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Munificence (उदारता, दानशीलता) = great generosity.</b><br><b>Munificense</b> is misspelt – the ending is '-cence', not '-cense'.<br><b>Apostrophize (संबोधित करना)</b> = to address someone absent in a speech – correct<br><b>Ethereal (अलौकिक)</b> = extremely light and delicate – correct<br><b>Penumbra (उपछाया)</b> = the partly shaded outer region of a shadow – correct<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Munificense.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":96,"local_id":"50096","quid":"Q1000072476","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"One Word Substitution","question":{"en":"Choose the correct <b>one-word substitute</b> for: 'A person who cannot be tired'. [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Infallible"},"2":{"en":"Invincible"},"3":{"en":"Indefatigable"},"4":{"en":"Incurable"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Indefatigable (अथक) = never tiring; persistent.</b><br><b>Infallible (अचूक)</b> = never making mistakes<br><b>Invincible (अजेय)</b> = too strong to be defeated<br><b>Incurable (असाध्य)</b> = that cannot be cured<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): Indefatigable.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":97,"local_id":"50097","quid":"Q1000072477","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Active Passive Voice","question":{"en":"<b>Change the following from active to passive:</b><br>Someone has sent me a gift. [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"I have been sent a gift."},"2":{"en":"A gift is sent to me."},"3":{"en":"A gift was sent to me."},"4":{"en":"I was sent a gift."}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: Present perfect active (has/have + V3) → has/have + been + V3; an indefinite agent ('someone') is dropped.</b><br>With two objects, the person object 'me' becomes the subject 'I' → 'I have been sent a gift'.<br>Passive: I <b>have been sent</b> a gift.<br>Option 2 – simple present passive<br>Option 3 – simple past passive<br>Option 4 – simple past passive<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): I have been sent a gift.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":98,"local_id":"50098","quid":"Q1000072478","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Sentence Improvement","question":{"en":"Choose the most suitable option to replace the highlighted part of the sentence:<br>He <b><i>told that he will come</i></b> later. [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"said he would come"},"2":{"en":"told that he would came"},"3":{"en":"said that he would come"},"4":{"en":"said that he will come"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: 'told' needs a person object ('told me'); without one, use 'said'. After a past reporting verb, 'will' becomes 'would'.</b><br>Correct sentence: He <b>said that he would come</b> later.<br>said he would come – grammatical, but 'that' is dropped from the original pattern; option 3 keeps it as the formal standard<br>told that he would came – 'told' without object and 'would came' (modal + V2)<br>said that he will come – 'will' not changed to 'would'<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): said that he would come.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":99,"local_id":"50099","quid":"Q1000072479","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Sentence Improvement","question":{"en":"Choose the most suitable option to replace the highlighted part of the sentence:<br>The students <b><i>enjoyed to play in the rain.</i></b> [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"enjoyed play in the rain"},"2":{"en":"were enjoying play"},"3":{"en":"enjoyed playing in the rain"},"4":{"en":"enjoyed to be playing"}},"answer":"3","solution":{"en":"<b>Rule: 'enjoy' is followed by a gerund (V-ing), not a to-infinitive.</b><br>Correct sentence: The students <b>enjoyed playing</b> in the rain.<br>enjoyed play – bare verb after 'enjoyed'<br>were enjoying play – 'play' used wrongly and 'in the rain' dropped<br>enjoyed to be playing – to-infinitive after 'enjoy'<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (3): enjoyed playing in the rain.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false},{"no":100,"local_id":"50100","quid":"Q1000072480","section":"ENGLISH","topic":"Antonym","question":{"en":"<b>Choose the most appropriate antonym of the underlined word.</b><br><br>The committee’s <b><u>admonition</u></b> regarding the safety breach was taken seriously by the staff. [SSC CGL 06/10/26 Shift 2]"},"options":{"1":{"en":"Commendation"},"2":{"en":"Counsel"},"3":{"en":"Forewarning"},"4":{"en":"Reprimand"}},"answer":"1","solution":{"en":"<b>Admonition (चेतावनी, फटकार) = a firm warning or reprimand.</b><br><b>Commendation (प्रशंसा)</b> = formal praise ✔<br><b>Counsel (सलाह)</b> = advice – close to admonition<br><b>Forewarning (पूर्व चेतावनी)</b> – synonym<br><b>Reprimand (फटकार)</b> – synonym<br>More antonyms: praise, approval, applause.<br><br><b>Hence, the correct answer is option (1): Commendation.</b>"},"marks":{"correct":2,"negative":0.5},"has_image":false}]}}};